{"id": "8", "pred": "The key difference between metoprolol tartrate and metoprolol succinate lies in their duration of action and release mechanisms. Metoprolol succinate is the long-acting, extended-release form of metoprolol that remains in the bloodstream for 24 hours, allowing it to be taken only once a day. In contrast, metoprolol tartrate is the short-acting, immediate-release form that does not stay in the bloodstream for a full 24 hours, requiring it to be taken at least twice a day. Chemically, succinate is derived from succinic acid, while tartrate is derived from tartaric acid. Additionally, metoprolol succinate is associated with side effects like constipation and dry mouth due to its dehydrating effect, whereas metoprolol tartrate may cause diarrhea and sleep-related issues such as insomnia or unusual dreams.", "raw_output": "The key difference between metoprolol tartrate and metoprolol succinate lies in their duration of action and release mechanisms. Metoprolol succinate is the long-acting, extended-release form of metoprolol that remains in the bloodstream for 24 hours, allowing it to be taken only once a day. In contrast, metoprolol tartrate is the short-acting, immediate-release form that does not stay in the bloodstream for a full 24 hours, requiring it to be taken at least twice a day. Chemically, succinate is derived from succinic acid, while tartrate is derived from tartaric acid. Additionally, metoprolol succinate is associated with side effects like constipation and dry mouth due to its dehydrating effect, whereas metoprolol tartrate may cause diarrhea and sleep-related issues such as insomnia or unusual dreams.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between tartate and succinate is their chemical derivation: succinate is derived from succinic acid while tartrate is derived from tartaric acid. Additionally, succinate is an extended-release drug that stays in the bloodstream for 24 hours, making it a once-per-day pill. On the other hand, tartrate is an immediate-release drug that does not stay in the bloodstream for 24 hours and needs to be taken at regular intervals. Another important difference is that succinate has a greater dehydrating effect and may cause side effects like constipation and dry mouth, whereas tartrate may cause diarrhea and sleep issues like insomnia or unusual dreams.", "question": "what is the difference between tartate and succinate", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 63.827, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 1376, 6672, 1948, 2270, 453, 1080, 337, 12183, 376, 349, 323, 2270, 453, 1080, 337, 20038, 3277, 15448, 304, 862, 8090, 315, 1917, 323, 4879, 23783, 13, 6212, 453, 1080, 337, 20038, 3277, 374, 279, 1293, 12, 34922, 11, 11577, 44724, 1352, 315, 2270, 453, 1080, 337, 429, 8458, 304, 279, 99116, 369, 220, 17, 19, 4115, 11, 10693, 432, 311, 387, 4429, 1172, 3055, 264, 1899, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 2270, 453, 1080, 337, 12183, 376, 349, 374, 279, 2805, 12, 34922, 11, 13922, 44724, 1352, 429, 1558, 537, 4717, 304, 279, 99116, 369, 264, 2480, 220, 17, 19, 4115, 11, 22703, 432, 311, 387, 4429, 518, 3245, 10917, 264, 1899, 13, 18994, 2673, 11, 20038, 3277, 374, 14257, 504, 20038, 92335, 13621, 11, 1393, 12183, 376, 349, 374, 14257, 504, 44815, 277, 292, 13621, 13, 22406, 11, 2270, 453, 1080, 337, 20038, 3277, 374, 5815, 448, 3108, 6239, 1075, 733, 48586, 323, 9058, 10780, 4152, 311, 1181, 409, 25172, 1095, 2456, 11, 19853, 2270, 453, 1080, 337, 12183, 376, 349, 1231, 5240, 68293, 323, 6084, 13904, 4714, 1741, 438, 82411, 476, 18511, 18707, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0334, -0.828, -0.3133, -0.0, -0.0009, 0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.024, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0182, 0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.1605, -0.0002, -0.0194, -0.0148, -0.0111, -0.0035, -0.4175, -0.3831, -0.775, -0.0495, -0.0601, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0153, -0.05