{"id": "20", "pred": "Note: The passages do not provide detailed cooking times or temperatures, but the setup and preparation steps are", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to grill a porterhouse:\n\n1. Set up the grill for three-zone grilling. If using a charcoal grill, dump a chimney of lit coals into the grill. Spread the coals into a double layer at the far side and a single layer in the center, leaving the section closest to you coal-free. Replace the grill grate. If using a gas grill, set it up for three-zone grilling.\n\n2. Keep the grill hot, clean, and lubricated. When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil.\n\n3. Place the porterhouse steak on the grill. Due to its size and thickness, use the three-zone setup: sear the steak over direct heat (hot zone), then move it to the indirect heat (cool zone) to finish cooking evenly without burning the exterior.\n\n4. The porterhouse steak includes a NY Strip on one side of the bone and a filet on the other. Cooking it just right will provide tremendous flavor from the bone and a tender, juicy result.\n\nNote: The passages do not provide detailed cooking times or temperatures, but the setup and preparation steps are", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nThe provided passages do not contain any information or instructions on how to grill a Porterhouse steak specifically. While they do provide general guidance on setting up a grill and preparing the grill grate, they do not offer any specific advice or steps for cooking a Porterhouse steak. Therefore, I cannot provide a response based on the given passages.", "question": "how to grill a porterhouse", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 83.283, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 389