{"id": "24", "pred": "Magellan of Virginia hosts weekly Provider Q&A Sessions every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., which are open to all providers to address their questions and issues. These calls continue until further notice. Magellan administers behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs and partners with members, providers, and stakeholders to elevate the quality and satisfaction in healthcare delivery.", "raw_output": "Magellan of Virginia hosts weekly Provider Q&A Sessions every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., which are open to all providers to address their questions and issues. These calls continue until further notice. Magellan administers behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs and partners with members, providers, and stakeholders to elevate the quality and satisfaction in healthcare delivery.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nMagellan of Virginia does offer continuing education clock hours/credits for their e-learning courses. According to passage 1, Magellan is approved to offer CE clock hours/credits by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB).\n\nAdditionally, Magellan of Virginia has been selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. This is mentioned in passage 2.\n\nFinally, Magellan of Virginia offers a Provider Q&A Session every Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. for providers to address their questions and issues. This is mentioned in passage 3.", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 29.854, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids"