{"id": "27", "pred": "Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, remove the door stop on the striker side and top using a chisel. Reinstall the door stop 1/4 inch back from its original position using the paint or stain", "raw_output": "To fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\n\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry it up until it comes loose. Remove it, and also remove the door stop on top.\n3. Place the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. Use the line in the paint, stain, or varnish to align it properly.\n4. Nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on.\n5. Tighten the hinge screws first.\n6. Enlarge the strike plate hole or move the strike plate if the latch doesn’t align with the hole in the strike plate.\n7. Perform the “lipstick test” if misalignment isn’t clearly visible to determine where adjustments are needed.\n\nAfter these adjustments, the door should shut and lock normally.\n\nAnswer: Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, remove the door stop on the striker side and top using a chisel. Reinstall the door stop 1/4 inch back from its original position using the paint or stain", "gt": "To fix a door that won't lock, first try to align the door latch with the hole in the strike plate. If the latch is misaligned, you can perform a lipstick test to see where the latch contacts the strike plate. If it contacts too high or too low, tighten all the door's hinge screws. You may also need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb or move the strike plate. If this doesn't work, shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb, pry it up until it comes loose and remove it. Replace the door stop back on the jamb, set back 1/4 inch from its original location. Nail the side and top piece of 