{"id": "33", "pred": "To cook pollock, preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet, optionally layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices, and spray the baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray if desired. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Optionally, after the fish is cooked, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, return to the oven, and allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.", "raw_output": "To cook pollock, preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet, optionally layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices, and spray the baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray if desired. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Optionally, after the fish is cooked, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, return to the oven, and allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.", "gt": "To cook pollock, first preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper and place them on the baking sheet. Layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which should take about 15 minutes. If desired, turn the oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet and return fish to the oven to allow cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 44.387, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 855, 19963, 