{"id": "38", "pred": "To cook pollock, preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet, optionally layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices, and spray the baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray if desired. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Optionally, after the fish is cooked, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, return to the oven, and allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.", "raw_output": "To cook pollock, preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet, optionally layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices, and spray the baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray if desired. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Optionally, after the fish is cooked, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, return to the oven, and allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to cook pollock:\n\nPreheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper or aluminum foil. You can also add sliced onions, green peppers, and tomatoes on top of the fillets. Bake for 15 minutes or until the fish flakes easily with a fork. If desired, top with cheese and return to the oven for an additional 3 minutes or until the cheese is melted.\n\nTherefore, the answer is not \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 44.35, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 