{"id": "44", "pred": "Alternatively, if the plastic is difficult to remove:\n- Use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic, then attempt to peel it off.\n- If complete removal is not possible, consider replacing the drum or the entire dryer and consult a service technician for the repair.", "raw_output": "To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the softened plastic off using a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, being careful not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the affected area to dissolve the plastic.\n4. Wipe the area with a damp cloth to rinse off the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again.\n6. Rinse thoroughly with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n\nAlternatively, if the plastic is difficult to remove:\n- Use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic, then attempt to peel it off.\n- If complete removal is not possible, consider replacing the drum or the entire dryer and consult a service technician for the repair.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to remove plastic from a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again.\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n\nIf the plastic does not come off with this method, another option is to use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic until it becomes soft and pliable. Then, attempt to peel it off carefully. However, be aware that this method may not work, and in that case, replacing the drum or the entire dryer may be necessary. It is recommended to call a service technician for this type of repair.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to get plastic out of clothes dryer is:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper.\n3. Apply nail polish remover to dissolve the plastic.\n4. Rinse with a damp cloth and soap solution.\n5. Use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic if necessary.\n\nIf the plastic still does not come off, consider replacing the drum or the entire dryer.", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 66.976, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 633, 12188, 700, 315, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 6452, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 624, 17, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 89058, 12188, 1007, 1667, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 1660, 16585, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 92100, 315, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 11495, 3082, 311, 72639, 279, 12188, 624, 19, 13, 467, 3444, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 1007, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 624, 20, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 41284, 315, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 3015, 13, 55047, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 323, 10273, 279, 3082, 1549, 624, 21, 13, 57368, 325, 26364, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 382, 92014, 11, 421, 279, 12188, 374, 5000, 311, 4057, 510, 12, 5443, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 311