{"id": "47", "pred": "These steps are part of preparing the quilt, likely for mitered binding, as outlined in the tutorial.", "raw_output": "To fold a quilt as described in the passage, follow these steps:\n\n1. Lay your quilt on a flat surface such as a bed or table.\n2. Fold the lower right corner up toward the center of the quilt, ensuring the fold is on the bias.\n3. Fold the lower left corner up toward the center of the quilt, again making sure the fold is on the bias.\n4. Fold the top left corner down toward the center of the quilt, maintaining the bias fold.\n5. Finally, fold the top right corner down toward the center of the quilt, ensuring the fold is on the bias.\n\nThese steps are part of preparing the quilt, likely for mitered binding, as outlined in the tutorial.", "gt": "To fold a quilt, follow these steps:\n\n1. Lay the quilt on a flat surface such as a bed or table.\n2. Fold the lower right corner up towards the center of the quilt, ensuring the fold is on the bias.\n3. Fold the lower left corner up towards the center of the quilt, again on the bias.\n4. Fold the top left corner down towards the center of the quilt, again on the bias.\n5. Finally, fold the top right corner down towards the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is also on the bias.", "question": "how to fold a quilt", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 48.353, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 11555, 264, 60736, 438, 7481, 304, 279, 21085, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 43924, 697, 60736, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 1741, 438, 264, 4845, 476, 1965, 624, 17, 13, 60473, 279, 4722, 1290, 9131, 705, 8841, 279, 4126, 315, 279, 60736, 11, 22573, 279, 11555, 374, 389, 279, 15470, 624, 18, 13, 60473, 279, 4722, 2115, 9131, 705, 8841, 279, 4126, 315, 279, 60736, 11, 1549, 3259, 2704, 279, 11555, 374, 389, 279, 15470, 624, 19, 13, 60473, 279, 1909, 