{"id": "57", "pred": "These methods help prevent birds from nesting, which is important because bird nests can block ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and droppings can transmit disease.", "raw_output": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch in several ways:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch using a staple gun. If your porch has open rafters, staple the netting to the top of the porch. The netting prevents birds from accessing spaces where they often build nests.\n\n2. Install bird netting over the top of light fixtures to block birds' access. Choose nonflammable netting safe around light bulbs and ensure it is installed so it does not entangle birds.\n\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch. The sight of a predator can scare birds away. Move the plastic hawk periodically so birds do not become accustomed to it and it remains effective.\n\nThese methods help prevent birds from nesting, which is important because bird nests can block ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and droppings can transmit disease.", "gt": "To prevent birds from building a nest on your porch, you can attach bird netting to the eves and top of your porch with staples. Additionally, you can install bird netting over your light fixture to deter birds from accessing it. Another option is to mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds away. It's important to note that any product used to deter birds should be nonflammable and safe to use.", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 60.618, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [2610, 646, 2506, 19654, 504, 4752, 264, 22791, 389, 697, 44647, 304, 3807, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 48384, 11958, 4179, 1280, 311, 279, 384, 4693, 2163, 279, 46342, 3