{"id": "60", "pred": "These methods help prevent birds from nesting, which is important because bird nests can block ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and droppings can transmit disease.", "raw_output": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch in several ways:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch using a staple gun. If your porch has open rafters, staple the netting to the top of the porch. The netting prevents birds from accessing spaces where they often build nests.\n\n2. Install bird netting over the top of light fixtures to block birds' access. Choose nonflammable netting safe around light bulbs and ensure it is installed so it does not entangle birds.\n\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch. The sight of a predator can scare birds away. Move the plastic hawk periodically so birds do not become accustomed to it and it remains effective.\n\nThese methods help prevent birds from nesting, which is important because bird nests can block ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and droppings can transmit disease.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building a nest on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun.\n2. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it.\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds away.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to keep birds from building a nest on your porch is:\n\nAttach bird netting to the eaves or install bird netting over the light fixture, and/or mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch.", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 60.588, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "t