{"id": "63", "pred": "This will set the selected browser as the default for opening hyperlinks and web links in Windows 7.", "raw_output": "To set the default web browser in Windows 7, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Settings app by either opening the Start menu and clicking the Settings icon or using the keyboard shortcut Windows + I.\n2. Click on the first option titled \"System\" (which includes display, notifications, apps, and power settings).\n3. In the left-pane, click on \"Default apps.\"\n4. On the right-side of the screen, scroll down to locate the \"Web browser\" section.\n5. Click on the current default browser entry (such as Edge or another browser other than Chrome), which will reveal the \"Choose an app\" option.\n6. Select the browser you want to set as default (e.g., Google Chrome) from the list.\n\nThis will set the selected browser as the default for opening hyperlinks and web links in Windows 7.", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here are the steps to set the default browser to Windows:\n\nMethod 1:\n\n1. Open the Settings app by clicking the Start menu and then clicking the Settings icon, or by using the Windows + I keyboard shortcut.\n2. In the Settings app, click the first option titled System (display, notifications, apps, power).\n3. In the left-pane, click Default apps.\n4. On the right-side, scroll down the page to see Web browser section.\n5. Click on the Edge browser entry (or any browser other than Chrome) to reveal Choose an app, and then click Google Chrome to set it as default browser.\n\nAlternatively, you can also set Mozilla Firefox as your default Windows browser by following these steps:\n\n1. Open your Firefox browser.\n2. Click on the Firefox menu button, represented by three horizontal lines and located in the upper right-hand corner of the browser window.\n3. When the pop-out menu appears, select Options.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "question": 