{"id": "77", "pred": "1. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding during cooking.\n2. Combine the bratwurst, onions, butter, and beer in a large stock pot.\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n4. Preheat a grill for medium-high heat and lightly oil the grate.\n5. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly.\n6. Alternatively, you can boil or simmer the bratwurst in a beer mixture with onions, red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper, then finish on the grill for added flavor and browning.\n7. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "raw_output": "To cook brats, follow these steps:\n\n1. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding during cooking.\n2. Combine the bratwurst, onions, butter, and beer in a large stock pot.\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n4. Preheat a grill for medium-high heat and lightly oil the grate.\n5. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly.\n6. Alternatively, you can boil or simmer the bratwurst in a beer mixture with onions, red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper, then finish on the grill for added flavor and browning.\n7. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "gt": "To cook brats, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n4. Place the bratwurst in a large pot with onions, butter, and beer.\n5. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n6. Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and continue cooking on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally.\n7. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "question": "how to cook brats", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset"