0.3325, -0.3128, -0.0109], "cumulative_logprob": -20.5973, "norm_logp": -0.1503, "input_len": 305, "output_tokens": 137, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.62, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "105", "pred": "The body systems work together by supporting and maintaining each other's functions—such as the urinary system cleaning blood and removing waste from other systems, and the respiratory system providing oxygen and removing carbon dioxide from various systems.", "raw_output": "The body systems work together to maintain normal functioning. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from multiple systems including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. Similarly, the respiratory system supplies oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from systems such as the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These interactions show how closely interconnected the body's systems are in supporting overall health and function. Answer: The body systems work together by supporting and maintaining each other's functions—such as the urinary system cleaning blood and removing waste from other systems, and the respiratory system providing oxygen and removing carbon dioxide from various systems.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how the body systems work together:\n\n1. The skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, and nervous systems all work together to help keep the body functioning normally. (Passage 1)\n2. The urinary system works closely with all other systems of the body to clean blood from the body and remove waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. (Passage 2)\n3. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the body systems work together in the following ways:\n\n* The skeletal system provides support and structure for the body, while the muscular system helps move the body and its parts.\n* The digestive system breaks down food into nutrients that can be absorbed and used by the body, while the respiratory system provides oxygen for energy production.\n* The circulatory system delivers oxygenated blood to the body's cells and removes carbon dioxide, while the urinary system removes waste products from the blood.\n* The endocrine system produces hormones that regulate various bodily functions, including growth and development, metabolism, and reproductive processes.\n* The lymphatic system helps defend the body against infection and disease, while the immune system fights off foreign invaders.\n* The nervous system controls and coordinates the body's functions, including movement, sensation, and thought processes.\n\nOverall, the body's systems work together in a complex interplay to maintain homeostasis and ensure the proper functioning of the body.", "question": "how the body systems work together", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 45.698, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 311, 10306, 4622, 30201, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 3871, 504, 5248, 5942, 2670, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 34239, 11, 279, 41531, 1849, 16720, 23552, 311, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 504, 5942, 1741, 438, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 4220, 21880, 1473, 1246, 15148, 82316, 279, 2487, 594, 5942, 525, 304, 12613, 8084, 2820, 323, 729, 13, 21806, 25, 576, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 553, 12613, 323, 20337, 1817, 1008, 594, 5746, 2293, 20805, 438, 279, 71635, 1849, 15826, 6543, 323, 17592, 12291, 504, 1008, 5942, 11, 323, 279, 41531, 1849, 8241, 23552, 323, 17592, 12499, 39489, 504, 5257, 5942, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.049, -0.048, -0.0016, -0.0006, -0.0005, -0