{"id": "106", "pred": "The body systems work together by supporting and maintaining each other's functions—such as the urinary system cleaning blood and removing waste from other systems, and the respiratory system providing oxygen and removing carbon dioxide from various systems.", "raw_output": "The body systems work together to maintain normal functioning. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from multiple systems including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. Similarly, the respiratory system supplies oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from systems such as the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These interactions show how closely interconnected the body's systems are in supporting overall health and function. Answer: The body systems work together by supporting and maintaining each other's functions—such as the urinary system cleaning blood and removing waste from other systems, and the respiratory system providing oxygen and removing carbon dioxide from various systems.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together as follows:\n\nThe skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, and reproductive systems all work together to help keep the body functioning normally. The urinary system helps to clean waste products from the other systems, while the respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the other systems. The nervous system plays a crucial role in coordinating the functions of all the other systems.", "question": "how the body systems work together", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 45.546, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 311, 10306, 4622, 30201, 13, 1752, 3110, 1