{"id": "119", "pred": "The name Teresa means \"Reap\" in Greek and American contexts, \"Harvester\" in Italian, and refers to two popular saints in Spanish. It is derived from the Greek word “therizein,” meaning “to harvest, harvester,” or possibly from “theros,” meaning “summer.”", "raw_output": "The name Teresa has multiple meanings across different cultures:\n\n- In Greek, the meaning of Teresa is \"Reap\" or \"from Therasia.\"\n- In American context, it also means \"Reap; from Therasia.\"\n- In Italian, the meaning is \"Harvester.\"\n- In Spanish, it is associated with the names of two popular saints: 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux.'\n\nEtymologically, Teresa is thought to come from the Greek “therizein,” meaning “to harvest, harvester,” or from the Greek “theros,” meaning “summer.” Therasia is also the name of a Greek island and is linked to the origin of the name.\n\nAnswer: The name Teresa means \"Reap\" in Greek and American contexts, \"Harvester\" in Italian, and refers to two popular saints in Spanish. It is derived from the Greek word “therizein,” meaning “to harvest, harvester,” or possibly from “theros,” meaning “summer.”", "gt": "The name Teresa is of Greek, American, Italian, and Spanish origin. In Greek and American, it means 'Reap; from Therasia.' In Italian, it is interpreted as 'Harvester.' In Spanish, the name is associated with two popular saints, 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux.' The name is also thought to originate from the Greek “therizein” meaning “to harvest, harvester” or from the Greek “theros” meaning “summer”.", "question": "teresa name meaning", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 68.105, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 829, 63440, 702, 5248, 49700, 3941, 2155, 26735, 1447, 12, 758, 17860, 11, 279, 7290, 315, 63440, 374, 330, 693, 391, 1, 476, 330, 1499, 663, 9247, 685, 10