{"id": "120", "pred": "The name Teresa means \"Reap\" in Greek and American contexts, \"Harvester\" in Italian, and refers to two popular saints in Spanish. It is derived from the Greek word “therizein,” meaning “to harvest, harvester,” or possibly from “theros,” meaning “summer.”", "raw_output": "The name Teresa has multiple meanings across different cultures:\n\n- In Greek, the meaning of Teresa is \"Reap\" or \"from Therasia.\"\n- In American context, it also means \"Reap; from Therasia.\"\n- In Italian, the meaning is \"Harvester.\"\n- In Spanish, it is associated with the names of two popular saints: 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux.'\n\nEtymologically, Teresa is thought to come from the Greek “therizein,” meaning “to harvest, harvester,” or from the Greek “theros,” meaning “summer.” Therasia is also the name of a Greek island and is linked to the origin of the name.\n\nAnswer: The name Teresa means \"Reap\" in Greek and American contexts, \"Harvester\" in Italian, and refers to two popular saints in Spanish. It is derived from the Greek word “therizein,” meaning “to harvest, harvester,” or possibly from “theros,” meaning “summer.”", "gt": "The name Teresa is of Greek origin and means \"Reap; from Therasia\" or \"Harvester\". It is also a Spanish and Italian name and is associated with two popular saints, Teresa of Avila and Therese of Lisieux. The name Theresa is a variation of Teresa and also means \"Reaper; from Therasia\". The etymology of the name is uncertain, but it is thought to come from the Greek words \"therizein\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester\" or \"theros\" meaning \"summer\".", "question": "teresa name meaning", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 67.958, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 829, 63440, 702, 5248, 49700, 3941, 2155, 26735, 1447, 12, 758, 17860, 11, 279, 7290, 315, 63440, 374, 330, 6