{"id": "123", "pred": "The name Teresa means \"Reap\" in Greek and American contexts, \"Harvester\" in Italian, and refers to two popular saints in Spanish. It is derived from the Greek word “therizein,” meaning “to harvest, harvester,” or possibly from “theros,” meaning “summer.”", "raw_output": "The name Teresa has multiple meanings across different cultures:\n\n- In Greek, the meaning of Teresa is \"Reap\" or \"from Therasia.\"\n- In American context, it also means \"Reap; from Therasia.\"\n- In Italian, the meaning is \"Harvester.\"\n- In Spanish, it is associated with the names of two popular saints: 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux.'\n\nEtymologically, Teresa is thought to come from the Greek “therizein,” meaning “to harvest, harvester,” or from the Greek “theros,” meaning “summer.” Therasia is also the name of a Greek island and is linked to the origin of the name.\n\nAnswer: The name Teresa means \"Reap\" in Greek and American contexts, \"Harvester\" in Italian, and refers to two popular saints in Spanish. It is derived from the Greek word “therizein,” meaning “to harvest, harvester,” or possibly from “theros,” meaning “summer.”", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the meaning of the name Teresa is:\n\n* Reap; from Therasia (Greek)\n* Reaper; from Therasia (American)\n* Harvester (Italian)\n* Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux' (Spanish)\n\nIt is also mentioned that the name Teresa is a Greek baby name, an American baby name, an Italian baby name, and a Spanish baby name.\n\nTherefore, the meaning of the name Teresa can vary depending on the culture and language, but it generally means \"reaper\" or \"harvester\", and is also associated with the names of two popular saints.", "question": "teresa name meaning", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 67.976, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_