{"id": "126", "pred": "1. Prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids to the required length—either 70 2/4 inches (as per passage 1) or 6 feet (as per passage 2). Position and level the skids according to the shed plans.\n3. For the floor framing:\n   - Cut two rim joists—either two pressure-treated 2 x 4s to 6 feet (passage 3) or two 2 x 6 rim joists to 7 3/4 inches (passage 1).\n   - Cut six joists to 44 3/4 inches (passage 1).\n   - Assemble the floor frame and set it on the skids.\n   - Check for squareness, then anchor the frame to the skids using joist clip angles (passage 1) or toenail floor joists directly to the skids (passage 2).\n4. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame (passage 2).\n5. The walls are built", "raw_output": "To build a lean-to shed, follow these steps based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids to the required length—either 70 2/4 inches (as per passage 1) or 6 feet (as per passage 2). Position and level the skids according to the shed plans.\n3. For the floor framing:\n   - Cut two rim joists—either two pressure-treated 2 x 4s to 6 feet (passage 3) or two 2 x 6 rim joists to 7 3/4 inches (passage 1).\n   - Cut six joists to 44 3/4 inches (passage 1).\n   - Assemble the floor frame and set it on the skids.\n   - Check for squareness, then anchor the frame to the skids using joist clip angles (passage 1) or toenail floor joists directly to the skids (passage 2).\n4. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame (passage 2).\n5. The walls are built", "gt": "Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site, cutting and assembling the skids, flooring, and walls. To prepare the site, a 4\" layer of compacted gravel is recommended. The skids are cut to 70 2/4\" and set and leveled according to the shed building plans. Two 2 x 6 rim joists are cut at 7 3/4\" and six joists at 44 3/4\". The floor is assembled and set on the skids, checked for square, and anchored to the skids with four joist clip angles. The walls are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. Pressure-treated 4 by 4s are used for the skids, while 2 by 4s are used for the rim joists and flooring. 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood is attached to the frame for the flooring.", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 82.152, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1936, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 3118, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 2747, 553, 34644, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 624, 17, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 19, 856, 220, 19, 1901, 3365, 311, 279, 2567, 3084, 2293, 49898, 220, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 14924, 320, 300, 817, 21085, 220, 16, 8, 476, 220, 21, 7541, 320, 300, 817, 21085, 220, 17, 568, 12380, 323, 2188, 279, 1901, 3365, 4092, 311, 279, 24354, 6649, 624, 18, 13, 1752, 279, 6422, 57949, 510, 256, 481, 19649, 1378, 30130, 7647, 1671, 2293, 49898, 1378, 7262, 87086, 220, 17, 856, 220, 19, 82, 311, 220, 21, 7541, 320, 6385, 424, 220, 18, 8, 476, 1378, 220, 17, 856, 220, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 311, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 320, 6385, 424, 220, 16, 4292, 256, 481, 19649, 4743, 7647, 1671, 311, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 320, 6385, 424, 220, 16, 4292, 256, 481, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 4034, 323, 738, 432, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 624, 256, 481, 4248, 369, 9334, 2090, 11, 1221, 17105, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 1667, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 320, 6385, 424, 220, 16, 8, 476, 99034, 604, 6422, 7647, 1671, 5961, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 320, 6385, 424, 220, 17, 4292, 19, 13, 48384, 220, 18, 14, 19, 24241, 24459, 9777, 2371, 299, 994, 87898, 36148, 8630, 279, 4034, 320, 6385, 424, 220, 17, 4292, 20, 13, 576, 14285, 52