{"id": "129", "pred": "1. Prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids to the required length—either 70 2/4 inches (as per passage 1) or 6 feet (as per passage 2). Position and level the skids according to the shed plans.\n3. For the floor framing:\n   - Cut two rim joists—either two pressure-treated 2 x 4s to 6 feet (passage 3) or two 2 x 6 rim joists to 7 3/4 inches (passage 1).\n   - Cut six joists to 44 3/4 inches (passage 1).\n   - Assemble the floor frame and set it on the skids.\n   - Check for squareness, then anchor the frame to the skids using joist clip angles (passage 1) or toenail floor joists directly to the skids (passage 2).\n4. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame (passage 2).\n5. The walls are built", "raw_output": "To build a lean-to shed, follow these steps based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids to the required length—either 70 2/4 inches (as per passage 1) or 6 feet (as per passage 2). Position and level the skids according to the shed plans.\n3. For the floor framing:\n   - Cut two rim joists—either two pressure-treated 2 x 4s to 6 feet (passage 3) or two 2 x 6 rim joists to 7 3/4 inches (passage 1).\n   - Cut six joists to 44 3/4 inches (passage 1).\n   - Assemble the floor frame and set it on the skids.\n   - Check for squareness, then anchor the frame to the skids using joist clip angles (passage 1) or toenail floor joists directly to the skids (passage 2).\n4. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame (passage 2).\n5. The walls are built", "gt": "What are the dimensions of the shed in passage 3?\n\nThe dimensions of the shed in passage 3 are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide.", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 82.385, 