{"id": "130", "pred": "3. Bilateral Relations:\n   - India supported Vietnam’s independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War.\n   - India supported North Vietnam during the war without engaging in military hostilities.\n   - India and Vietnam maintain strong bilateral relations with cultural and economic links dating back to the 2nd century, including influence from the Indic Chăm Pa kingdom on Vietnamese", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passages, here are the differences between Vietnam and India:\n\n1. Education Trends and Equity:\n   - India's education trends are described as \"much more typical,\" focusing initially on getting children into school by establishing resources, facilities, schools, and training teachers.\n   - Vietnam's education system is relatively equitable, meaning poorer children receive the same educational opportunities as wealthier children, so they are not disadvantaged within the school system.\n\n2. Colonial History and Decolonization:\n   - India gained independence from the United Kingdom in 1947.\n   - Vietnam (as part of French Indochina) lost its colonial status to France shortly after World War II in 1945.\n   - Following decolonization, India experienced division among Hindus, Muslims, and Sikhs, leading to conflicts, while the passages do not mention similar post-colonial divisions in Vietnam.\n\n3. Bilateral Relations:\n   - India supported Vietnam’s independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War.\n   - India supported North Vietnam during the war without engaging in military hostilities.\n   - India and Vietnam maintain strong bilateral relations with cultural and economic links dating back to the 2nd century, including influence from the Indic Chăm Pa kingdom on Vietnamese", "gt": "The passages suggest that trends in India are more typical than those in Vietnam, particularly in the area of education. Vietnam's education system is described as relatively equitable, where poorer children receive the same treatment as their better-off counterparts. In contrast, India's early focus was on getting children into school, which involved setting up schools, and training teachers. Politically, India supported Vietnam's independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War. Both countries have a history of colonialism, with India being a former colony of the United Kingdom and Vietnam of France. Post-colonization, India experienced division and conflict among Hindus, Muslims and Sikhs. Cultural and economic links between India and Vietnam date back to the 2nd century.", "question": "difference between vietnam and india", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 82.581, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 1588, 525, 279, 11799, 1948, 22500, 323, 6747, 1447, 16, 13, 11668, 49630, 323, 57488, 510, 256, 481, 6747, 594, 6731, 18339, 525, 7481, 438, 330, 58078, 803, 14260, 1335, 21080, 15102, 389, 3709, 2841, 1119, 2906, 553, 30592, 4963, 11, 12786, 11, 8682, 11, 323, 4862, 13336, 624, 256, 481, 22500, 594, 6731, 1849, 374, 12040, 76009, 11, 7290, 65181, 2841, 5258, 279, 1852, 16229, 10488, 438, 11939, 1268, 2841, 11, 773, 807, 525, 537, 79847, 2878, 279, 2906, 1849, 382, 17, 13, 72748, 11099, 323, 3714, 72269, 2022, 510, 256, 481, 6747, 18163, 23665, 504, 279, 3639, 15072, 304, 220, 16, 24, 19, 22, 624, 256, 481, 22500, 320, 300, 949, 315, 8585, 2263, 4953, 2210, 8, 5558, 1181, 36583, 2639, 311, 9625, 19620, 1283, 4337, 5004, 7946, 304, 220, 16, 24, 19, 20, 624, 256, 481, 22713, 1622, 72269, 2022, 11, 6747, 10321, 12804, 4221, 81629, 11, 19503, 11, 323, 77349, 4997, 11, 6388, 311, 25800, 11, 1393, 279, 46769, 653, 537, 6286, 4428, 1736, 19459, 263, 530, 36501, 304, 22500, 382, 18, 13, 38058, 19165, 31367, 510, 256, 481, 6747, 7248, 22500, 748, 23665, 504