{"id": "132", "pred": "The roasting time depends on clove size and may take up to 45 minutes to an hour for larger cloves.", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passage, to roast garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Prepare the whole garlic bulb by peeling and discarding the papery outer layers, while keeping the skins of the individual cloves intact.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of the cloves, exposing the individual garlic cloves.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up (a muffin pan is suggested to prevent rolling).\n5. Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head and use your fingers to rub the oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n\nThe roasting time depends on clove size and may take up to 45 minutes to an hour for larger cloves.", "gt": "Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, but keep the skins of the individual cloves intact. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves to expose them. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves. Season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices if you like. Roasting time is dependent on the size of the cloves and may take up to 45 minutes or an hour for larger cloves. Once roasted, the garlic cloves can be stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 57.693, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 21085, 11, 311, 57685, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19,