{"id": "135", "pred": "The roasting time depends on clove size and may take up to 45 minutes to an hour for larger cloves.", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passage, to roast garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Prepare the whole garlic bulb by peeling and discarding the papery outer layers, while keeping the skins of the individual cloves intact.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of the cloves, exposing the individual garlic cloves.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up (a muffin pan is suggested to prevent rolling).\n5. Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head and use your fingers to rub the oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n\nThe roasting time depends on clove size and may take up to 45 minutes to an hour for larger cloves.", "gt": "Here are brief answers to the question on how to roast individual garlic cloves based on the provided passages:\n\nPassage 1: The passage does not provide information on how to roast individual garlic cloves specifically. However, it does mention that larger garlic cloves may take up to an hour to soften when roasted, so it is possible to assume that smaller cloves will take less time.\n\nPassage 2: This passage provides some options for seasoning the garlic before roasting, but it does not provide instructions on how to roast individual garlic cloves.\n\nPassage 3: This passage provides a method for roasting entire garlic heads, but it does not address how to roast individual garlic cloves. The passage does mention that cutting the top of the garlic bulb and exposing the individual cloves can help them roast more evenly, but it does not provide specific instructions on how to do this.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "p