{"id": "137", "pred": "The roasting time depends on clove size and may take up to 45 minutes to an hour for larger cloves.", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passage, to roast garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Prepare the whole garlic bulb by peeling and discarding the papery outer layers, while keeping the skins of the individual cloves intact.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of the cloves, exposing the individual garlic cloves.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up (a muffin pan is suggested to prevent rolling).\n5. Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head and use your fingers to rub the oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n\nThe roasting time depends on clove size and may take up to 45 minutes to an hour for larger cloves.", "gt": "To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n6. Roast in the preheated oven for 45 minutes to an hour, or until the cloves are softened.\n7. Store roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.\n\nYou can also season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices before roasting.", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 57.555, "s