{"id": "146", "pred": "To sew", "raw_output": "To sew a zipper gusset, follow these steps:\n\n1. Trace all pattern pieces to the rest of the fabric and cut.\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper, 1/4″ away from the center, with right sides facing each other.\n4. Change the presser foot to a zipper foot and sew a line near the seam line to secure the position.\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top with right side facing down and stitch on the seam line.\n6. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset and top stitch near the seam line.\n7. Repeat the process for the other side of the zipper gusset.\n8. Ensure the width of the zipper between the gusset measures 1/2″.\n9. Change the presser foot back to the normal foot and stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so the main and lining fabrics attach together nicely.\n10. For applications like a pencil case, lightly clip the piping seam allowance at curves, align the zipper gusset with center markings on the body, and sew from marking to marking at both ends.\n\nAnswer: To sew", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to sew a zipper gusset:\n\n1. Make a casing in the side seams by stitching the outer edge of the gusset and the back side seam.\n2. Slide the boning right down into the casing.\n3. Push the seam allowance to the back and tack the casing to the lining, if necessary, so it doesn't move.\n4. Make a zipper sandwich by placing one piece of lining fabric face up, followed by the zipper, and then the outer fabric right side facing down.\n5. Sew across the top of the zipper sandwich with a zipper foot, making sure to line up the three edges.\n6. Repeat the process for the other side of the zipper.\n7. Trace all pattern pieces to the remaining fabric and cut them out.\n8. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper, with the right sides facing each other, and sew a line near the seam line to secure the position.\n9. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the zipper gusset, with the right sides facing down, and stitch along the seam line.\n10. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset and top stitch near the seam line.\n11. Repeat the process for the other side of the zipper gusset.\n12. The width of the zipper between the gusset should measure 1/2\".\n13. Change the presser foot back to a normal foot and stitch along the seam allowance around the zipper gusset to attach the main and lining fabrics together nicely.\n\nTherefore, to sew a zipper gusset, you need to make a casing in the side seams, insert the boning, make a zipper sandwich, sew the zipper gusset to the zipper, and attach the lining to the zipper gusset.", "question": "how to sew a zipper gusset", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 83.141, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 22352, 264, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 27163, 678, 5383, 9666, 311, 279, 2732, 315, 279, 13055, 323, 3931, 624, 17, 13, 7405, 264, 2421, 61936, 3143, 279, 1909, 2936, 315, 279, 68761, 624, 18, 13, 17471, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 311, 279, 68761, 11, 220, 16, 14, 19, 21580, 3123, 504, 279, 4126, 11, 448, 1290, 11067, 12880, 1817, 1008, 624, 19, 13, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 311, 264, 68761, 4478, 323, 22352, 264, 1555, 3143, 279, 26396, 1555, 311, 9767, 279, 2309, 624, 20, 13, 10771, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 35371, 389, 1909, 448, 1290, 3108, 12880, 1495, 323, 32861, 389, 279, 26396, 1555, 624, 21, 13, 40284, 279, 35371, 311, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 1887, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 323, 1909, 32861, 3143, 279, 26396, 1555, 624, 22, 13, 44801, 279, 1882, 369, 279, 1008, 3108, 315, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 624, 23, 13, 29279, 279, 2374, 315, 279, 68761, 1948, 279, 342, 355, 746, 10953, 220, 16, 14, 17, 21580, 624, 24, 13, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 1182, 311, 279,