{"id": "150", "pred": "Note: The term \"bake\" is not used in the passages; the method described is boiling, not baking.", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make hard-boiled eggs:\n\n1. Place cold eggs in a single layer in a pan.\n2. Pour in enough cold water to cover the eggs by about 1 inch.\n3. Place the pan on the stove over high heat.\n4. As soon as the water comes to a boil, turn off the heat, cover the pan, and remove it from the heat.\n5. Let the eggs sit in the hot water until fully cooked: approximately 9 minutes for medium eggs, 12 minutes for large eggs, and 15 minutes for extra-large eggs.\n6. After cooking, pour out the hot water and cover the eggs with cold water to stop the cooking process.\n\nNote: The term \"bake\" is not used in the passages; the method described is boiling, not baking.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to bake hard-boiled eggs:\n\n1. Place cold eggs in a single layer in a pan with enough cold water to cover them by about 1 inch.\n2. Place the pan on the stove over high heat.\n3. As soon as the water comes to a boil, turn the heat off, cover the pan, and remove it from the heat.\n4. Allow the eggs to sit in the water for the appropriate amount of time, depending on the size of the eggs (9 minutes for medium, 12 minutes for large, and 15 minutes for extra-large).\n\nNote: Do not peek during the cooking process, and do not worry if the eggs are not perfectly symmetrical or have a slightly greenish-gray yolk.", "question": "how to bake hard boiled egg", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 57.105, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 2588, 69466, 2181, 18805, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 9255, 18805, 304, 264, 3175, 6193, 304, 264, 7215, 624, 17, 13, 25968, 304, 3322, 9255, 3015, 311, 3421, 279, 18805, 553,