{"id": "167", "pred": "6. **Add color and clarity**: Use color to make your graph visually appealing and easier to", "raw_output": "To make a graph for your research, especially a bar graph which is useful for comparing categories, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Collect your data**: Gather all the information you want to represent. For example, if you're analyzing rainfall, collect data on how many inches of rain occurred each month.\n\n2. **Choose the right type of graph**: Decide whether a bar graph or another type (like a line or pie chart) is best. Bar graphs are ideal for comparing groups or types, such as rainfall across different months or salaries in different states.\n\n3. **Title your graph**: Give your graph a clear and descriptive title that reflects what it represents.\n\n4. **Set up the axes**: \n   - The x-axis (horizontal) will typically show the categories you are comparing (e.g., months from February 2005 to February 2006).\n   - The y-axis (vertical) will have a scale showing the values (e.g., inches of rainfall). Each bar’s height should be proportionate to the value it represents.\n\n5. **Draw the bars**: Create rectangular bars for each category, making sure their heights accurately reflect the data.\n\n6. **Add color and clarity**: Use color to make your graph visually appealing and easier to", "gt": "To create a graph for your research, you first need to collect all of your data, remembering that the graph should show a comparison among categories. If you are creating a bar graph, you will use rectangular bars to represent different values. You need to title your graph and determine how high your graph needs to go. If your data points are substantially different in scale, you can use a pie chart. The y-axis of your graph will have a scale, and each bar’s height should be proportionate to the size of the category it represents. Make sure to consider any disproportionate responses that might impact the scale of your graph. Regardless of the type of graph you choose, it should provide a clear visual representation of your information.", "question": "show me how can i make gragh for my research", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 82.676, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 264, 4771, 369, 697, 3412, 11, 5310, 264, 3619, 4771, 892, 374, 5390, 369, 26297, 11059, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 47504, 697, 821, 95518, 48995, 678, 279, 1995, 498, 1366, 311, 4009, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 421, 498, 2299, 41018, 52858, 11, 6530, 821, 389, 1246, 1657, 14924, 315, 11174, 10017, 1817, 2254, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 24051, 279, 1290, 943, 315, 4771, 95518, 98881, 3425, 264, 3619, 4771, 476, 2441, 943, 320, 4803, 264, 1555, 476, 4349, 9487, 8, 374, 1850, 13, 4716, 38999, 525, 10507, 369, 26297, 5203, 476, 4494, 11, 1741, 438, 52858, 3941, 2155, 3951, 476, 36432, 304, 2155, 5302, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 3851, 697, 4771, 95518, 20678, 697, 4771, 264, 2797, 323, 52844, 2265, 429, 25963, 1128, 432, 10868, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 1649, 705, 279, 24745, 95518, 715, 256, 481, 576, 856, 35321, 320, 30629, 8, 686, 11136, 1473, 279, 11059, 498, 525, 26297, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 3951, 504, 7400, 220, 17, 15, 15, 20, 311, 7400, 220, 17, 15, 15, 21, 4292, 256, 481, 576, 379, 35321, 320, 15292, 8, 686, 614, 264, 5452, 9027, 279, 2750, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 14924, 315, 52858, 568, 8886, 3619, 748, 2608, 1265, 387, 21117, 349, 311, 279, 897, 432, 10868, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 8137, 279, 15904, 95518, 4230, 51424, 15904, 369, 1817, 5582, 11, 3259, 2704, 862, 35294, 29257, 8708, 279, 821, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 2212, 1894, 323, 31273, 95518, 5443, 1894, 311, 1281, 697, 4771, 42295, 32252, 323, 8661, 311], "logp_list": [-0.528, -0.0182, -0.0, -0.5763, -0.0021, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0048, -0.8802, -0.0467, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.5152, -0.0007, -0.8116, -0.0028, -0.4576, -0.2193, -0.0377, -0.0113, -0.0001, -0.0396, -0.2089, -0.