{"id": "180", "pred": "The psychological effects of hugging include making individuals feel good, fostering emotional intimacy, improving relationships, and even leading to happy marriages. Empathic listening can create a \"psychological hug,\" making the conversation partner feel embraced. Additionally, hugging—whether with another person or an inanimate object like a teddy bear—helps soothe existential fears and reduces worry about mortality.", "raw_output": "The psychological effects of hugging include making individuals feel good, fostering emotional intimacy, improving relationships, and even leading to happy marriages. Empathic listening can create a \"psychological hug,\" making the conversation partner feel embraced. Additionally, hugging—whether with another person or an inanimate object like a teddy bear—helps soothe existential fears and reduces worry about mortality.", "gt": "Hugging has significant psychological effects. It creates a warm feeling that affects the entire body, akin to the effect of many drugs operating simultaneously. This could be due to the feeling of a loving embrace, leading to good relationships and emotional intimacy. It also enhances empathy and listening skills, which can lead to a psychological hug. Furthermore, research has found that hugging can significantly reduce worries about mortality and boost self-esteem. This soothing effect can be achieved even when hugging an inanimate object like a teddy bear.", "question": "psychological effects of hugging", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 27.212, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 23187, 6239, 315, 305, 35268, 2924, 3259, 7775, 2666, 1661, 11, 85544, 14269, 65164, 11, 18392, 11871, 11, 323, 1496, 6388, 311, 6247, 46351, 13, 13409, 587, 292, 14289, 646, 1855, 264, 330, 91009, 5729, 29784, 1335, 3259, 279, 10435, 8263, 2666, 42503, 13, 2240