{"id": "183", "pred": "1. Allow the roast to stand at room temperature for at least 1 hour.\n2. Preheat the oven either to 375°F (as mentioned in Passage 1) or to 450°F (as mentioned in Passages 2 and 3). If using 450°F, allow the oven to preheat for a minimum of 15 minutes.\n3. Season the roast. According to Passage 2, use only a small amount of salt and lots of fresh ground black pepper—avoid other spices to preserve the prime rib's flavor. Alternatively, Passage 1 mentions rubbing the roast with House Seasoning.\n4. Place the roast on a rack in the pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up.\n5. Roast the prime rib. If using 375°F, roast for 1 hour (as per Passage 1). If using 450°F, the initial high-heat searing is typically done for about 15–20 minutes to develop a crust, followed by lowering the temperature to finish cooking (though this specific step is not fully detailed in the passages).\n6. After roasting,", "raw_output": "To cook a small prime rib roast in the oven, follow these steps:\n\n1. Allow the roast to stand at room temperature for at least 1 hour.\n2. Preheat the oven either to 375°F (as mentioned in Passage 1) or to 450°F (as mentioned in Passages 2 and 3). If using 450°F, allow the oven to preheat for a minimum of 15 minutes.\n3. Season the roast. According to Passage 2, use only a small amount of salt and lots of fresh ground black pepper—avoid other spices to preserve the prime rib's flavor. Alternatively, Passage 1 mentions rubbing the roast with House Seasoning.\n4. Place the roast on a rack in the pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up.\n5. Roast the prime rib. If using 375°F, roast for 1 hour (as per Passage 1). If using 450°F, the initial high-heat searing is typically done for about 15–20 minutes to develop a crust, followed by lowering the temperature to finish cooking (though this specific step is not fully detailed in the passages).\n6. After roasting,", "gt": "Before cooking the prime rib roast, let it stand at room temperature for at least 1 hour. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Season the roast with a small amount of salt and lots of fresh ground black pepper. Place the roast on a rack in a pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up. Roast it in the oven for 1 hour. After cooking, you can prepare au jus by placing the roasting pan on the stove over high heat. Add wine and cook for 8-10 minutes, stirring and scraping any brown bits. Add beef stock and cook to reduce the juice by half, which might take about 20 minutes. Add salt and pepper to taste.", "question": "how to cook a small prime rib roast in oven", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 82.5, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 264, 2613, 10250, 20131, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 26530, 279, 57685, 311, 2498, 518, 3054, 9315, 369, 518, 3245, 220, 16, 6460, 624, 17, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 2987, 311, 220, 18, 22, 20, 58472, 320, 300, 9733, 304, 98475, 220, 16, 8, 476, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 320, 300, 9733, 304, 9970, 1134, 220, 17, 323, 220, 18, 568, 1416, 1667, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 11, 2138, 279, 23387, 311, 855, 19963, 369, 264, 8028, 315, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 18, 13, 14263, 279, 57685, 13, 10548, 311, 98475, 220, 17, 11, 990, 1172, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 12021, 323, 10077, 315, 7722, 4910, 3691, 24353, 2293, 47856, 1008, 48559, 311, 21129, 279, 10250, 20131, 594, 17172, 13, 38478, 11, 98475, 220, 16, 33845, 55935, 279, 57685, 448, 4678, 14263, 287, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 57685, 389, 264, 29659, 304, 279, 7215, 448, 279, 20131, 3108, 1495, 323, 279, 38985, 3108, 705, 624, 20, 13, 11830, 559, 279, 10250, 20131, 13, 1416, 1667, 220, 18, 22, 20, 58472, 11, 57685, 369, 220, 16, 6460, 320, 300, 817, 98475, 220, 16, 568, 1416, 1667, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 11, 279, 2856, 1550, 12, 19963, 511, 3249, 374, 11136, 2814, 369, 9