{"id": "189", "pred": "Based on passage 1 and passage 2, chicken in a crock pot can be cooked on low for 6–8 hours until done. Alternatively, it can be cooked on high for 1 hour followed by low for about 5 hours until done. Passage 3 also supports that cooking chicken breasts on low for 8 hours in a slow cooker will make them tender, and that cooking for 4 hours on high also works fine as long as there is enough moisture. Therefore, the time required to make chicken tender in a crock pot ranges from 4 hours on high to 8 hours on low, depending on the setting used.", "raw_output": "Based on passage 1 and passage 2, chicken in a crock pot can be cooked on low for 6–8 hours until done. Alternatively, it can be cooked on high for 1 hour followed by low for about 5 hours until done. Passage 3 also supports that cooking chicken breasts on low for 8 hours in a slow cooker will make them tender, and that cooking for 4 hours on high also works fine as long as there is enough moisture. Therefore, the time required to make chicken tender in a crock pot ranges from 4 hours on high to 8 hours on low, depending on the setting used.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the answer to the question \"How long does it take to make chicken tender in a crock pot?\" is:\n\n6-8 hours on low heat, or 4 hours on high heat if you're short on time.\n\nThe first passage suggests cooking the chicken on low for 6-8 hours, or 1 hour on high and then 5 hours on low. The second passage repeats the same information. The third passage provides additional information that chicken breast will always come out tender as long as there is enough moisture, and suggests cooking it for 4 hours on high if you're short on time.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is 6-8 hours on low heat, or 4 hours on high heat if you're short on time.", "question": "how long does it take to make chicken tender in crock pot", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "ha