{"id": "210", "pred": "Elements are pure substances made of one type of atom.", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passages, here are the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures:\n\n1. Elements: Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom (all atoms have the same number of protons).\n\n2. Compounds: \n   - Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements chemically bonded together.\n   - They are pure substances.\n   - The elements in a compound cannot be separated by physical means; chemical methods are required.\n\n3. Mixtures:\n   - Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts are not chemically bonded and retain their own identity.\n   - No new compound is formed when elements and compounds mix to form a mixture.\n   - Mixtures have a variable composition.\n   - The constituents show the properties of the individual substances.\n   - The components of a mixture can be easily separated by physical methods.\n   - Example: The atmosphere is a mixture.\n\nIn summary, elements are pure substances made of one type of atom, compounds are chemically bonded combinations of elements forming a pure substance, and mixtures are physically combined substances that can be easily separated and retain the properties of their components.\n\nAnswer: Elements are pure substances made of one type of atom.", "gt": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom, meaning all the atoms in an element have the same number of protons. Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. The individual components of a mixture can be physically separated from each other. Mixtures have variable compositions and show the properties of their constituent substances. Elements and compounds just mix together to form a mixture and no new compound is formed.", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 82.703, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 1588, 525, 279, 11799, 1948, 5424, 11, 31146, 11, 323, 6514, 18513, 1447, 16, 13, 34157, 25, 34157, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 323, 525, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 320, 541, 32199, 614, 279, 1852, 1372, 315, 462, 34411, 3593, 17, 13, 13317, 3095, 25, 715, 256, 481, 13317, 3095, 525, 32055, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 8424, 2673, 69141, 3786, 624, 256, 481, 2379, 525, 10526, 32055, 624, 256, 481, 576, 5424, 304, 264, 23628, 4157, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 26, 11483, 5413, 525, 2567, 382, 18, 13, 19219, 18513, 510, 256, 481, 19219, 18513, 525, 6961, 27459, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 14060, 862, 1828, 9569, 624, 256, 481, 2308, 501, 23628, 374, 14122, 979, 5424, 323, 31146, 6514, 311, 1352, 264, 20980, 624, 256, 481, 19219, 18513, 614, 264, 3890, 18037, 624, 256, 481, 576, 50620, 1473, 279, 5888, 315, 279, 3842, 32055, 624, 256, 481, 576, 6813, 315, 264, 20980, 646, 387, 6707, 18663, 553, 6961, 5413, 624, 256, 481, 13383, 25, 576, 16566, 374, 264, 20980, 382, 641, 12126, 11, 5424, 525, 10526, 32055, 1865, 315, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 11, 31146, 525, 8424, 2673, 69141, 27459, 315, 5424, 29064, 264, 10526, 19699, 11, 323, 6514, 18513, 525, 21893, 10856, 32055, 429, 646, 387, 6707, 18663, 323, 14060, 279, 5888, 315, 862, 6813, 382, 16141, 25, 34157, 525, 10526, 32055, 1865, 315, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 13], "logp_list": [-0.595, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.4253, -0.002, -0.0605, -0.0957, -0.0003, -0.0043, -0.1351, -0.0032, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.