{"id": "213", "pred": "Elements are pure substances made of one type of atom.", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passages, here are the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures:\n\n1. Elements: Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom (all atoms have the same number of protons).\n\n2. Compounds: \n   - Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements chemically bonded together.\n   - They are pure substances.\n   - The elements in a compound cannot be separated by physical means; chemical methods are required.\n\n3. Mixtures:\n   - Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts are not chemically bonded and retain their own identity.\n   - No new compound is formed when elements and compounds mix to form a mixture.\n   - Mixtures have a variable composition.\n   - The constituents show the properties of the individual substances.\n   - The components of a mixture can be easily separated by physical methods.\n   - Example: The atmosphere is a mixture.\n\nIn summary, elements are pure substances made of one type of atom, compounds are chemically bonded combinations of elements forming a pure substance, and mixtures are physically combined substances that can be easily separated and retain the properties of their components.\n\nAnswer: Elements are pure substances made of one type of atom.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are:\n\n* Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. They have a fixed composition and cannot be broken down into simpler substances by physical means.\n* Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements that are chemically bonded together. They have a fixed composition and are pure substances.\n* Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and retain their own identity. They have a variable composition and can be separated by physical means.\n\nTherefore, the key differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are their composition, bonding, and separability. Elements are homogeneous and have a fixed composition, compounds are heterogeneous and have a fixed composition, and mixtures are heterogeneous and have a variable composition. Additionally, elements and compounds are chemically bonded, while mixtures are not.", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 82.212, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 1588, 525, 279, 11799, 1948, 5424, 11, 31146, 11, 323, 6514, 18513, 1447, 16, 13, 34157, 25, 34157, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 323, 525, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 320, 541, 32199, 614, 279, 1852, 1372, 315, 462, 34411, 3593, 17, 13, 13317, 3095, 25, 715, 256, 481, 13317, 3095, 525, 32055, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 8424, 2673, 69141, 3786, 624, 256, 481, 2379, 525, 10526, 32055, 624, 256, 481, 576, 5424, 304, 264, 23628, 4157, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 26, 11483, 5413, 525, 2567, 382, 18, 13, 19219, 18513, 510, 256, 481, 19219, 18513, 525, 6961, 27459, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 14060, 862, 1828, 9569, 624, 256, 481, 2308, 501, 23628, 374, 14122, 979, 5424, 323, 31146, 6514, 311, 1352, 264, 20980, 624, 256, 481, 19219, 18513, 614, 264, 3890, 18037, 624, 256, 481, 576, 50620, 1473, 279, 5888, 315, 279, 3842, 32055, 624, 256, 481, 576, 6813, 315, 264, 20980, 646, 387, 6707, 18663, 553, 6961, 5413, 624, 256, 481, 13383, 25, 576, 16566, 374, 264, 20980, 382, 641, 12126, 11, 5424, 525, 10526, 32055, 1865, 315, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 11, 31146,