{"id": "226", "pred": "If the toilet flushes slowly, tighten the chain slightly on the lift arm.", "raw_output": "To fix the lift valve (flapper valve and chain) in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Connect the new chain to the third hole on the lift arm—the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm—using pliers to secure it firmly.\n5. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included, tighten it securely until there is no more give.\n6. Turn the water valve back on to fill the tank.\n7. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n8. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n9. Once satisfied with the operation, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n\nIf the toilet flushes slowly, tighten the chain slightly on the lift arm.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to fix a lift valve in a toilet:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve and any remaining pieces of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Install the new flapper valve and connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, making sure it is securely fastened.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to test for correct operation.\n5. Adjust the chain as needed to ensure a proper flush. Cut off any excess chain to prevent tangling.\n\nNote: If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 67.955, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 3