{"id": "231", "pred": "Oil stains on concrete driveways are nearly impossible to avoid but can be cleaned using various methods depending on the size of the spill and how long the stain has set. Recommended approaches include using commercial-grade cleaners followed by scrubbing with a brush or broom, then using detergent in a pressure washer while maintaining an even pace and consistent nozzle distance to prevent streaking. Alternative methods compared in one video include oven cleaner, Goop hand cleaner, and carburetor cleaner. For fresh or stubborn small stains, the poultice method may be effective. Prior to cleaning, wash off dirt and debris with water from a hose or bucket, but avoid high-pressure hoses as they may push the oil deeper into the pavement.", "raw_output": "Oil stains on concrete driveways are nearly impossible to avoid but can be cleaned using various methods depending on the size of the spill and how long the stain has set. Recommended approaches include using commercial-grade cleaners followed by scrubbing with a brush or broom, then using detergent in a pressure washer while maintaining an even pace and consistent nozzle distance to prevent streaking. Alternative methods compared in one video include oven cleaner, Goop hand cleaner, and carburetor cleaner. For fresh or stubborn small stains, the poultice method may be effective. Prior to cleaning, wash off dirt and debris with water from a hose or bucket, but avoid high-pressure hoses as they may push the oil deeper into the pavement.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question \"How do you remove oil stains from a concrete driveway?\"\n\nTo remove oil stains from a concrete driveway, you can use one of the following methods:\n\n1. Oven cleaner, goop hand cleaner, and carburetor cleaner (as mentioned in Passage 1).\n2. A commercial-grade cleaner applied with a brush or broom, followed by scrubbing with a pressure washer (as described in Passage 3).\n\nBefore starting the cleaning process, it is recommended to wash away any dirt or debris from the affected area (Passage 2). Additionally, it is important to avoid using high-pressure hoses to clean the stain, as this can push the oil deeper into the pavement (Passage 2).\n\nIt is also noted that the size of the oil spill and the length of time the stain has been present will affect the method of removal (Passage 3). For small and stubborn stains, the poultice method may be effective (Passage 2).", "question": "oil stain on concrete driveway", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 47.464, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [76909, 62463, 389, 14175, 39255, 69271, 525, 7009, 11997, 311, 5648, 714, 646, 387, 27722, 1667, 5257, 5413, 11649, 389, 279, 1379, 315, 279, 38797, 323, 1246, 1293, 279, 51964, 702, 738, 13, 50662, 19827, 2924, 1667, 8353, 40227, 74865, 8110, 553, 44901, 7132, 448, 264, 15625, 476, 2896, 316, 11, 1221, 1667, 90134, 304, 264, 7262, 52892, 1393, 20337, 458, 1496, 17857, 323, 12966, 81881, 6010, 311, 5358, 29214, 287, 13, 41109, 5413, 7707, 304, 825, 2766, 2924, 23387, 31881, 11, 5994, 453, 1424, 31881, 11, 323, 34772, 552, 10980, 31881, 13, 1752, 7722, 476, 51396, 2613, 62463, 11, 279, 16836, 4832, 558, 1714, 1231, 387, 7373, 13, 31399, 311, 15826, 11, 11369, 1007, 25284, 323, 33998, 448, 3015, 504, 264, 37500, 476, 15621, 11, 714, 5648, 1550, 88461, 95836, 438, 807, 1231, 4484, 279, 5590, 19117, 1119, 279, 64342, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.3149, -0.0, -0.0, -0.4741, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0828, -0.3976, -0.0233, 0.0, -0.0002, -0.5028, -0.0018, -0.0, -0.2207, -0.001, -0.4863, -0.0004, -0.0386, -0.0, -0.4825, -0.0069, -0.5248, 0.0, -0.0006, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0803, -0.0002, -0.1263, -0.8676, -0.0003, -0.6149, -0.2448, -0.0003, -0.0025, -1.0323, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0135, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0006, 0.0, 0.0, -0.244, 