{"id": "248", "pred": "One difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA covers more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Another key difference is in the definition of disability: under the ADA, a physical or mental impairment must substantially limit a major life activity to qualify as a disability, whereas under FEHA, only a limitation (not necessarily substantial) on a major life activity is required.", "raw_output": "One difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA covers more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Another key difference is in the definition of disability: under the ADA, a physical or mental impairment must substantially limit a major life activity to qualify as a disability, whereas under FEHA, only a limitation (not necessarily substantial) on a major life activity is required.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's a brief answer to the question:\n\nThe main difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to all employers in California, regardless of size or sector, while ADA applies to private employers with 4 to 15 employees and does not cover public employers. Additionally, FEHA has a broader definition of disability, requiring only that a mental or physical disability limit a major life activity, whereas ADA requires a substantial limitation.", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 31.334, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [3966, 6672, 1948, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 374, 429, 279, 78325, 16790, 311, 869, 10486, 22426, 448, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 11, 1393, 27931, 17020, 14521, 803, 8256, 323, 1558, 537, 32037, 1948, 