{"id": "250", "pred": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. Rinse pork chops, then sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with a spice mixture made of seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring. Use your hands to massage the spice rub into the meat and let it stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, cooking for about 12 minutes per side.", "raw_output": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. Rinse pork chops, then sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with a spice mixture made of seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring. Use your hands to massage the spice rub into the meat and let it stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, cooking for about 12 minutes per side.", "gt": "To grill pork chops according to allrecipes.com, preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring. Rinse the pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Massage the spice rub into the meat and let it stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat for about 12 minutes per side or until they are no longer pink inside.", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 34.598, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [4703, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 8628, 323, 33404, 5590, 279, 85354, 13, 57368, 325, 35067, 90078, 11, 1221, 84847, 279, 14401, 90078, 389, 2176, 11067, 448, 264, 41686, 20980, 1865, 315, 51514, 12021, 11, 3691, 24353, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 3