{"id": "256", "pred": "Using a lint brush with an extendable handle is recommended for effectively cleaning the inside of the pipe. Regular cleaning helps maintain dryer efficiency and prevents fire hazards.", "raw_output": "To clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it. If the vent duct isn't fastened or sealed, it should slide right out.\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole.\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n4. Use the dryer vent brush to clean lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\n\nAdditionally, for a more thorough cleaning:\n- Remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean that area.\n- Pay attention to the area around the lint filter.\n- Remove the lint filter frame to gain easier access to lint deposits, and use a vacuum nozzle for deeper cleaning.\n\nUsing a lint brush with an extendable handle is recommended for effectively cleaning the inside of the pipe. Regular cleaning helps maintain dryer efficiency and prevents fire hazards.", "gt": "To clean your dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Remove the outside cover on the vent.\n2. Use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe.\n3. If possible, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there as well.\n4. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter and clean it thoroughly.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 69.09, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4240, 264, 46622, 10378, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 95210, 279, 46622, 10378, 34