{"id": "271", "pred": "The earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy include mood swings due to hormonal changes, dizziness from dilated blood vessels and dropped blood pressure, bloating, spotting, cramping, and nausea or vomiting. Nausea and vomiting, commonly known as morning sickness, affect around half of all pregnant women and typically start around six weeks after the last period. Some women may also experience emotional changes and weepiness in early pregnancy. A missed period is a well-known indicator, but these other symptoms can also signal early pregnancy.", "raw_output": "The earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy include mood swings due to hormonal changes, dizziness from dilated blood vessels and dropped blood pressure, bloating, spotting, cramping, and nausea or vomiting. Nausea and vomiting, commonly known as morning sickness, affect around half of all pregnant women and typically start around six weeks after the last period. Some women may also experience emotional changes and weepiness in early pregnancy. A missed period is a well-known indicator, but these other symptoms can also signal early pregnancy.", "gt": "The earliest signs of pregnancy often include mood swings and unusual emotional behavior due to a flood of hormones in the body. Dizziness can also occur as pregnancy causes blood vessels to dilate and blood pressure to drop. Other early symptoms can include a missed period, bloating, spotting, and cramping. Approximately half of all pregnant women experience nausea and vomiting, and around 3 in 10 women experience nausea without vomiting, with these symptoms typically starting around six weeks after their last period.", "question": "earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 35.397, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 29658, 11929, 323, 13495, 315, 19636, 2924, 19