{"id": "276", "pred": "Severe osteoporosis refers to an advanced stage of the condition where significant bone density loss has already occurred, often without noticeable symptoms until severe damage is present. At this stage, the bones become extremely weak, leading to complications such as spinal compression fractures, which can happen even without a fall or injury. Symptoms of severe osteoporosis may include sudden, severe back pain that worsens when standing or walking, relief when lying down, loss of height over time, stooped posture, and fractures in the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other weight-bearing bones. Without treatment, individuals with severe osteoporosis are highly likely to suffer fractures, particularly in the spine or hips.", "raw_output": "Severe osteoporosis refers to an advanced stage of the condition where significant bone density loss has already occurred, often without noticeable symptoms until severe damage is present. At this stage, the bones become extremely weak, leading to complications such as spinal compression fractures, which can happen even without a fall or injury. Symptoms of severe osteoporosis may include sudden, severe back pain that worsens when standing or walking, relief when lying down, loss of height over time, stooped posture, and fractures in the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other weight-bearing bones. Without treatment, individuals with severe osteoporosis are highly likely to suffer fractures, particularly in the spine or hips.", "gt": "Severe osteoporosis is a condition characterized by significant bone density loss, resulting in weakened bones and increased risk of fractures. Symptoms may include sudden and severe back pain, loss of height over time, fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones. Without treatment, fractures, particularly in the spine or hips, are likely to occur.", "question": "what is severe osteoporosis", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "metho