{"id": "283", "pred": "Thus, the key difference lies in what they modify: adverb clauses modify verbs, adjectives, or adverbs, while adjective clauses modify nouns or pronouns.", "raw_output": "An adverb clause is a dependent clause that modifies a verb, adjective, or another adverb, most commonly a verb. It is introduced by subordinate conjunctions such as after, although, because, if, since, until, and while.\n\nIn contrast, an adjective clause modifies a noun or a pronoun and is introduced by a relative pronoun (who, whose, whom, which, that) or specific subordinate conjunctions (when and where).\n\nThus, the key difference lies in what they modify: adverb clauses modify verbs, adjectives, or adverbs, while adjective clauses modify nouns or pronouns.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, an adverb clause modifies a verb, adjective or another adverb, while an adjective clause modifies a noun or pronoun.", "question": "difference between an adverb clause and an adjective clause", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 41.947, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [2082, 993, 22328, 21647, 374, 264, 17749, 21647, 429, 82949, 264, 18607, 11, 84492, 11, 476, 2441, 993, 22328, 11, 1429, 16626, 264, 18607, 13, 1084, 374, 11523, 553, 78163, 31446, 82, 1741, 438, 1283, 11, 7892, 11, 1576, 11, 421, 11, 2474, 11, 3080, 11, 323, 1393, 382, 641, 12872, 11, 458, 84492, 21647, 82949, 264, 36921, 476, 264, 18613, 1624, 323, 374, 11523, 553, 264, 8674, 18613, 1624, 320, 14623, 11, 6693, 11, 8711, 11, 892, 11, 429, 8, 476, 3151, 78163, 31446, 82, 320, 9309, 323, 1380, 3593, 44500, 11, 279, 1376, 6672, 15448, 304, 1128, 807, 5602, 25, 993, 22328, 49098, 5602, 61846, 11, 993, 86578, 11, 476, 993, 54939, 11, 1393, 84492, 49098, 5602, 89838, 476, 18613, 58986, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2107, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0023, -0.0, -0.0003, 0.0, -0.0233, -0.23, 