{"id": "296", "pred": "Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity, and a baseball thrown by a pitcher, which has a large amount of kinetic energy despite its small mass because of its high velocity. Examples of potential energy include gravitational potential energy, which is the energy stored in an object due to its vertical position or height. Activities such as a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit demonstrate the presence of kinetic energy in motion.", "raw_output": "Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity, and a baseball thrown by a pitcher, which has a large amount of kinetic energy despite its small mass because of its high velocity. Examples of potential energy include gravitational potential energy, which is the energy stored in an object due to its vertical position or height. Activities such as a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit demonstrate the presence of kinetic energy in motion.", "gt": "Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane in flight, due to its large mass and fast velocity, and a baseball thrown by a pitcher, which can have a large amount of kinetic energy due to its fast velocity. Examples of potential energy include gravitational potential energy, which is the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, and elastic potential energy. Other activities like a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit also involve potential and kinetic energy.", "question": "what are examples of potential and kinetic energy?", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 36.872, 