{"id": "298", "pred": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump can be used. This pump sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater through a return line while simultaneously pulling hot water from the heater. This creates a continuous loop, ensuring that hot water is always available. Circulation can be managed using methods such as pushing a button, using a timer, or employing a motion sensor in demand systems.", "raw_output": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump can be used. This pump sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater through a return line while simultaneously pulling hot water from the heater. This creates a continuous loop, ensuring that hot water is always available. Circulation can be managed using methods such as pushing a button, using a timer, or employing a motion sensor in demand systems.", "gt": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is needed. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot, ensuring hot water is always available. Alternatively, recirculating pumps can be used to rapidly pull hot water from a water heater, while simultaneously sending cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. These systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or a motion sensor. However, it should be noted that heat loss from the pipes can occur, requiring the water heater to use more fuel.", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 30.161, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 11, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 646, 387, 1483