{"id": "300", "pred": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump can be used. This pump sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater through a return line while simultaneously pulling hot water from the heater. This creates a continuous loop, ensuring that hot water is always available. Circulation can be managed using methods such as pushing a button, using a timer, or employing a motion sensor in demand systems.", "raw_output": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump can be used. This pump sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater through a return line while simultaneously pulling hot water from the heater. This creates a continuous loop, ensuring that hot water is always available. Circulation can be managed using methods such as pushing a button, using a timer, or employing a motion sensor in demand systems.", "gt": "To make a hot water heater circulate, one can install a recirculation system. The system consists of a pump that pulls hot water from the water heater and simultaneously sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. This ensures that hot water is always available without having to wait for it to circulate naturally. Recirculation systems can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 30.087, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 11, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 646, 387, 1483, 13, 1096, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 504, 279, 4017, 3015, 5128, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 1393, 24303, 22266, 4017, 3015, 504, 279, 42238, 13, 1096, 11450, 264, 19259, 6337, 11, 22573, 429, 4017, 3015, 374, 2677, 2500, 13, 16338