{"id": "304", "pred": "Watermelons explode due to the buildup of gas inside from rotting. As the gas increases, pressure builds up within the watermelon. When the skin can no longer withstand the pressure, the watermelon explodes.", "raw_output": "Watermelons explode due to the buildup of gas inside from rotting. As the gas increases, pressure builds up within the watermelon. When the skin can no longer withstand the pressure, the watermelon explodes.", "gt": "Watermelons can explode due to external pressure, such as when a bunch of rubber bands are placed around the middle of the watermelon, causing potential energy to build up and eventually cause the watermelon to explode. Another cause of watermelon explosions is the buildup of gas inside the watermelon due to rotting. This increases the internal pressure and when the skin of the watermelon can no longer hold the gas inside, it will explode.", "question": "what causes watermelons to explode", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 16.791, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28253, 27127, 2382, 15758, 4152, 311, 279, 85665, 315, 6819, 4766, 504, 5749, 1280, 13, 1634, 279, 6819, 12703, 11, 7262, 22111, 705, 2878, 279, 3015, 71118, 13, 3197, 279, 6787, 646, 902, 5021, 50471, 279, 7262, 11, 279, 3015, 71118, 93913, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.117, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0021, 0.0, -0.0131, -0.0535, 0.0, -0.0127, -0.2633, -0.7975, -0.6218, -0.0, -0.1016, -0.0008, -0.0019, -0.0071, -0.2209, -0.0355, -0.5509, -0.0395, -0.0109, -0.3283, -0.0, -0.0057, -0.0, -0.0046, -0.0465, -0.0, -0.0454, -0.0873, -0.0, -0.0, -0.5522, -0.0142, -0.3906, -0.0, -0.1269, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0274, -0.528, -0.193], "cumulative_logprob": -5.2007, "norm_logp": -0.1182, "input_len": 335, "output_tokens": 44, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.52, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "