{"id": "318", "pred": "You can check if your taxes were filed by using methods such as the IRS2Go smartphone application, available for Apple users in the Apple App Store. Additionally, if you e-filed your taxes, you can wait 24 hours after the IRS acknowledged receipt of your return and then check the status online or through tax software that allows you to log in and view your return status. Providing your email address during the e-filing process often results in an email confirmation when the IRS accepts your return.", "raw_output": "You can check if your taxes were filed by using methods such as the IRS2Go smartphone application, available for Apple users in the Apple App Store. Additionally, if you e-filed your taxes, you can wait 24 hours after the IRS acknowledged receipt of your return and then check the status online or through tax software that allows you to log in and view your return status. Providing your email address during the e-filing process often results in an email confirmation when the IRS accepts your return.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, you can check the status of your tax return by:\n\n1. Using the IRS2Go app on your smartphone to check the status of your tax return online.\n2. Checking the status of your tax return over the phone by calling the IRS.\n3. Checking the status of your state tax return online or over the phone.\n\nTo check the status of your tax return, you will need your Social Security number, tax filing status, and the amount of any refund due. If you e-filed your return, you can check the status 24 hours after the IRS acknowledged receipt of your return. If you mailed your taxes, you will have to wait 3 or 4 weeks after mailing in your taxes.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to check taxes were filed is:\n\nYou can check the status of your tax return online or over the phone using the methods described above.", "question": "how can i check taxes were filed", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 34.545, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [2610, 646, 1779, 421, 697, 13125, 1033, 12729, 553, 1667, 5413, 1741, 438, 279, 33383, 17, 10850, 21511, 3766, 11, 2500, 369, 8162, 3847, 304, 279, 8162, 1845, 9129, 13, 22406, 11, 421, 498, 384, 14203, 67, 697, 13125, 11, 498, 646, 3783, 220, 17, 19, 4115, 1283, 279, 33383, 25498, 22567, 315, 697, 470, 323, 1221, 1779, 279, 2639, 2860, 476, 1526, 3742, 3162, 429, 6147, 498, 311, 1487, 304, 323, 1651, 697, 470, 2639, 13, 80100, 697, 2551, 2621, 2337, 279, 384, 2220, 7979, 1882, 3545, 3059, 304, 458, 2551, 19539, 979, 279, 33383, 26344, 697, 470, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0379, -0.0001, -0.0039, -0.2882, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.0006, -0.0003, -0.8575, -0.1931, -1.0181, -0.2577, -0.0, -0.7075, -0.0067, -0.0105, -0.0, -0.0573, -0.0298, -0.7614, -0.7856, -0.1813, -0.0041, -0.0, -1.3284, -0.0, -0.0086, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0707, -0.5744, -0.0001, -0.1633, -0.0017, -0.0988, -0.0001, -0.0198, -0.0105, -0.2701, -0.035, -0.7719, -0.2122, -0.6258, -0.0048, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0492, -0.0, -0.2614, -0.0008, -0.3659, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.5248, -0.3249, -0.0344, -0.4218, -0.0065, -0.0179, -0.6467, -0.2176, -0.3345, -0.0032, -0.3341, -0.9067, -0.3535, -0.0006, -0.0003, -0.5231, -0.3137, -0.4034, -0.2915, -0.0172, -0.2102, -0.0003, -0.8395, -0.0211, -0.2019, -0.0142, -0.4832, -0.5838, -0.7631, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0, -1.0892, -0.0962, -0.0, -0.2287, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.5785, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0067, -0.4747, -0.0625, -0.0568], "cumulative_logprob": -21.4649, "norm_logp": -0.2125, "input_len": 528, "output_tokens": 101, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.93, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "320", "pred": "The effect of a carbon footprint is to measure the environmental impact of your lifestyle by indicating the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases produced as a result of your daily activities. This measurement, typically in tons, reflects the total greenhouse gas emissions from various human activities such as heating homes, eating certain foods like cheeseburgers, and driving cars. High carbon footprints, such as the average of 20 tons per year in the U.S., contribute significantly to environmental issues like climate change.", "raw_output": "The effect of a carbon footprint is to measure the environmental impact of your lifestyle by indicating the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases produced as a result of your daily activities. This measurement, typically in tons, reflects the total greenhouse gas emissions from various human activities such as heating homes, eating certain foods like cheeseburgers, and driving cars. High carbon footprints, such as the average of 20 tons per year in the U.S., contribute significantly to environmental issues like climate change.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that the effect of a carbon footprint is a measure of the negative impact of human activities on the environment. The measurement of a carbon footprint typically indicates the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases produced through daily activities. Additionally, reducing one's carbon footprint can have a positive impact on the environment, even if the changes may seem small.", "question": "what is the effect of carbon footprint", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 34.021, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 2456, 315, 264, 12499, 42872, 374, 311, 6629, 279, 12158, 5421, 315, 697, 18899, 553, 18860, 279, 3311, 315, 12499, 39489, 323, 1008, 36547, 44512, 