{"id": "335", "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. Avoid yanking quickly to prevent leaving part of the tick’s mouth behind, which could cause an infection. Wear gloves if removing the tick with fingers. Additionally, check inside and behind the dog’s ears and around the eyes, as these are common tick hiding places. For prevention, use regular tick control products recommended by a veterinarian.", "raw_output": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. Avoid yanking quickly to prevent leaving part of the tick’s mouth behind, which could cause an infection. Wear gloves if removing the tick with fingers. Additionally, check inside and behind the dog’s ears and around the eyes, as these are common tick hiding places. For prevention, use regular tick control products recommended by a veterinarian.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how to get rid of ticks from dogs:\n\n1. Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, which are common hiding places for ticks. (Passage 1)\n2. Use tick control products recommended by a veterinarian to prevent ticks from attaching to the dog. (Passage 2)\n3. Remove ticks from the dog using a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. (Passage 1)\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages whether there are any specific products or methods for getting rid of ticks from dogs that are already infested.", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 35.646, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 990, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388,