{"id": "337", "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. Avoid yanking quickly to prevent leaving part of the tick’s mouth behind, which could cause an infection. Wear gloves if removing the tick with fingers. Additionally, check inside and behind the dog’s ears and around the eyes, as these are common tick hiding places. For prevention, use regular tick control products recommended by a veterinarian.", "raw_output": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. Avoid yanking quickly to prevent leaving part of the tick’s mouth behind, which could cause an infection. Wear gloves if removing the tick with fingers. Additionally, check inside and behind the dog’s ears and around the eyes, as these are common tick hiding places. For prevention, use regular tick control products recommended by a veterinarian.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to get rid of ticks from dogs:\n\n1. Check your dog's body thoroughly, especially in areas like inside and behind the ears, around the eyes, and other favorite tick hiding places.\n2. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and wear gloves if needed.\n3. Pull on the tick gently and steadily, making sure not to yank it away from your dog too quickly.\n4. Regularly use tick control products on your dog, as recommended by your veterinarian, to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog in the first place.\n\nIf you have any further questions or concerns, consult your veterinarian for advice.", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 35.736, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249,