{"id": "338", "pred": "Follow either the grilling or oven-cooking method as described, including preparation steps like removing the membrane, seasoning, and", "raw_output": "To make ribs, follow these steps:\n\n1. If grilling: Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F). Remove the ribs from foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, brush with sauce, cover, and cook for 5 minutes. Flip, brush again, and cook another 5 minutes. Continue flipping and brushing every 5 minutes until the sauce thickens and the ribs are heated through with grill marks—total grilling time is 20 minutes.\n\n2. If preparing for grilling or oven cooking: Lay the ribs on a rack in a single layer to allow heat circulation. Season by mixing mustard and liquid smoke (if using), brushing both sides, then sprinkling with a dry rub and patting gently to adhere.\n\n3. For oven-cooked BBQ ribs: Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs using a knife near the narrow end and pull it off in one piece. Place the ribs in a resealable bag and add enough BBQ sauce to cover. Line a baking pan with heavy-duty foil, overlapping generously to form a tent.\n\nAnswer: Follow either the grilling or oven-cooking method as described, including preparation steps like removing the membrane, seasoning, and", "gt": "To make ribs, start by removing the membrane from the bottom of the ribs with a knife. Place the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover them. Afterwards, line a baking pan with heavy duty foil. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer for heat circulation on all sides. Mix mustard and liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to make sure it adheres to the meat. To grill the ribs, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium and remove the ribs from the foil. Place them meaty-side up on the grill and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook for another 5 minutes. Continue this process until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through with grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "question": "how to make ribs", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 82.499, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 55149, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1416, 1081, 9400, 25, 26070, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 568, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 46399, 11, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 15625, 448, 19187, 11, 3421, 11, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 40284, 11, 15625, 1549, 11, 323, 4296, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 15003, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 3080, 279, 19187, 12045, 724, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 448, 39058, 15423, 2293, 5035, 1081, 9400, 882, 374, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 382, 17, 13, 1416, 20045, 369, 1081, 9400, 476, 23387, 17233, 25, 43924, 279, 55149, 389, 264, 29659, 304, 264, 3175, 6193, 311, 2138, 8628, 34755, 13, 14263, 553, 26792, 64307, 323, 14473, 16205, 320, 333, 1667, 701, 76726, 2176, 11067, 11, 1221, 50698, 2718, 448, 264, 9058, 10273, 323, 3272, 1280, 29273, 311, 48453, 382, 18, 13, 1752, 23387, 22471, 10823, 45277, 55149, 25, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 1667, 264, 21430, 3143, 279, 15026, 835, 323, 6815, 432, 1007, 304, 825, 6573, 13, 10771, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 323, 912, 3322, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 13, 7083, 264, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 54518, 46399, 11, 49817, 79120, 311, 1352, 264, 15632, 382, 16141, 25, 11112, 2987, 279, 1081, 9400, 476, 23387, 22471, 10746, 1714, 438, 7481, 11, 2670, 17975, 7354, 1075, 17592, 279, 38554, 11, 86219, 11, 323], "logp_list": [-0.3553, -0.0155, -0.0028, -0.3571, -0.4568, -0.0187, -0.016, -0.8468, -0.0697, -0.0, -0.9364, -0.047, -0.0, -