{"id": "340", "pred": "Follow either the grilling or oven-cooking method as described, including preparation steps like removing the membrane, seasoning, and", "raw_output": "To make ribs, follow these steps:\n\n1. If grilling: Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F). Remove the ribs from foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, brush with sauce, cover, and cook for 5 minutes. Flip, brush again, and cook another 5 minutes. Continue flipping and brushing every 5 minutes until the sauce thickens and the ribs are heated through with grill marks—total grilling time is 20 minutes.\n\n2. If preparing for grilling or oven cooking: Lay the ribs on a rack in a single layer to allow heat circulation. Season by mixing mustard and liquid smoke (if using), brushing both sides, then sprinkling with a dry rub and patting gently to adhere.\n\n3. For oven-cooked BBQ ribs: Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs using a knife near the narrow end and pull it off in one piece. Place the ribs in a resealable bag and add enough BBQ sauce to cover. Line a baking pan with heavy-duty foil, overlapping generously to form a tent.\n\nAnswer: Follow either the grilling or oven-cooking method as described, including preparation steps like removing the membrane, seasoning, and", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make ribs:\n\nTo grill the ribs:\n\n1. Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium temperature (350°F to 450°F).\n2. Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce.\n3. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes.\n4. Flip and brush the ribs and cook for another 5 minutes.\n5. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\n\nTo prepare the ribs before grilling:\n\n1. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer.\n2. Season the ribs by mixing the mustard and liquid smoke (if using), and brushing the ribs on both sides.\n3. Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\n\nFor oven-cooked BBQ ribs:\n\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag.\n3. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover the ribs.\n4. Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil.\n5. Place the ribs in the baking pan and bake at 350°F for 2-3 hours, or until the ribs are tender and the meat starts to pull away from the bone.", "question": "how to make ribs", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 82.382, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 55149, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1416, 1081, 9400, 25, 26070, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 568, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 46399, 11, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 15625, 448, 19187, 11, 3421, 11, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 40284, 11, 15625, 1549, 11, 323, 4296, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 15003, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 3080, 279, 19187, 12045, 724, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 448, 39058, 15423, 2293, 5035, 1081, 9400, 882, 374, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 382, 17, 13, 1416, 20045, 369, 1081, 9400, 476, 23387, 17233, 25, 43924, 279, 55149, 389, 264, 29659, 304, 264, 3175, 6193, 311, 2138, 8628, 34755, 13, 14263, 553, 26792, 64307, 323, 14473, 16205, 320, 333, 1667, 701, 76726, 2176, 11067, 11, 1221, 50698, 2718, 448, 264, 9058, 10273, 323, 3272, 1280, 29273, 311, 48453, 382, 18, 13, 1752, 23387, 22471, 10823, 45277, 55149, 25, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 1667, 264, 21430, 3143, 279, 15026, 835, 323, 6815, 432, 1007, 304, 825, 6573, 13, 10771, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 323, 912, 3322, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 13, 7083, 264, 27815,