{"id": "342", "pred": "Based on the provided passages, having a bowel movement does not result in meaningful weight loss related to body fat. While there may be a very small decrease in body weight due to the elimination of waste, this is not a loss of body fat. The passages clarify that body fat loss occurs through a calorie deficit, not from bowel movements. Additionally, the fat found in stools comes from unabsorbed dietary fat, not from the body's stored fat reserves. Therefore, any weight change from a bowel movement is temporary and not indicative of fat loss.", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passages, having a bowel movement does not result in meaningful weight loss related to body fat. While there may be a very small decrease in body weight due to the elimination of waste, this is not a loss of body fat. The passages clarify that body fat loss occurs through a calorie deficit, not from bowel movements. Additionally, the fat found in stools comes from unabsorbed dietary fat, not from the body's stored fat reserves. Therefore, any weight change from a bowel movement is temporary and not indicative of fat loss.", "gt": "While you may technically lose a small amount of weight after a bowel movement, this does not come from a loss of body fat. The decrease in body weight does not come from fat loss in stools, but rather from the elimination of undigested food and waste. Weight loss is primarily tied to your caloric intake and expenditure, not bowel movements. Unless your scale is highly accurate, you're unlikely to notice a difference in your body weight before and after a bowel movement.", "question": "when you have a bowel movement do you lose weight", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 37.684, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 3432, 264, 65258, 7203, 1558, 537, 1102, 304, 22414, 4680, 