-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "351", "pred": "Goodwill is important because it helps increase the customer base, retains existing clients, attracts investors, and makes the business more appealing to future buyers. It represents the value derived from the business's name and reputation, creating a lasting connection with customers that contributes to long-term success.", "raw_output": "Company goodwill refers to the intangible asset that arises from the positive reputation and strong relationship a business has with its customers. It includes the trust and loyalty customers develop when a company consistently provides good service or high-quality products. This leads to repeat business and word-of-mouth promotion, enhancing the company's attractiveness.\n\nGoodwill is important because it helps increase the customer base, retains existing clients, attracts investors, and makes the business more appealing to future buyers. It represents the value derived from the business's name and reputation, creating a lasting connection with customers that contributes to long-term success.", "gt": "Company goodwill is a business asset that is created when a business provides good service or product to their customers, leading to customer trust. This trust results in repeat customers and positive word-of-mouth, which can increase a company's customer base and retain old clients. Goodwill represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation of the business possesses. It is important because it can attract investors and future buyers, and it is an advantage of the reputation and connection with customers which tends to make that connection permanent.", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 39.022, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [14491, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 526, 60086, 9329, 429,