{"id": "367", "pred": "A rock is a large, heavy piece of earth material that is difficult to carry by hand, while a stone is a smaller, hand-carryable piece. Rocks are made of smaller stones, and stones can be used more easily in human activities like throwing.", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passages, the main differences between a rock and a stone are:\n\n1. Size and Portability: A rock is described as a large piece that is difficult to carry in the hand, whereas a stone is a smaller piece or pebble that can be easily carried in the hand.\n\n2. Composition: According to passage 3, rocks are made of smaller stones, and stones are derived from rocks.\n\n3. Usability: Stones can be pelted easily, but this is not possible with rocks.\n\nAdditionally, passage 1 suggests a symbolic or contextual difference: \"rock\" is often used metaphorically to represent something solid, substantial, or a foundation to place faith in (e.g., \"rock of one’s salvation\"), while \"stone\" more often implies human use.\n\nAnswer: A rock is a large, heavy piece of earth material that is difficult to carry by hand, while a stone is a smaller, hand-carryable piece. Rocks are made of smaller stones, and stones can be used more easily in human activities like throwing.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, a rock is defined as the hard material of the earth's crust that is normally exposed on the surface or underlying the soil. On the other hand, a stone is described as a smaller piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. The passages also mention that rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. Additionally, stones can be pelted easily, while rocks cannot. Therefore, the main difference between a rock and a stone is their size, with rocks being larger and stones being smaller and easier to handle.", "question": "what is the difference between a rock and a stone", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 70.145, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 279, 1887, 11799, 1948, 264, 6946, 323, 264, 9798, 525, 1447, 16, 13, 8478, 323, 5776, 2897, 25, 362, 6946, 374, 7481, 438, 264, 3460, 6573, 429, 374, 5000, 311, 6777, 304, 279, 1424, 11, 19853, 264, 9798, 374, 264, 9155, 6573, 476, 1051, 59880, 429, 646, 387, 6707, 11691, 304, 279, 1424, 382, 17, 13, 67106, 25, 10548, 311, 21085, 220, 18, 11, 23035, 525, 1865, 315, 9155, 26210, 11, 323, 26210, 525, 14257, 504, 23035, 382, 18, 13, 3985, 2897, 25, 56100, 646, 387, 281, 3818, 291, 6707, 11, 714, 419, 374, 537, 3204, 448, 23035, 382, 49574, 11, 21085, 220, 16, 13230, 264, 35296, 476, 65151, 6672, 25, 330, 20521, 1, 374, 3545, 1483, 45350, 2673, 311, 4009, 2494, 6437, 11, 11924, 11, 476, 264, 16266, 311, 1992, 9881, 304, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 330, 20521, 315, 825, 748, 44935, 3975, 1393, 330, 10812, 1, 803, 3545, 23945, 3738, 990, 382, 16141, 25, 362, 6946, 374, 264, 3460, 11, 8811, 6573, 315, 9393, 3684, 429, 374, 5000, 311, 6777, 553, 1424, 11, 1393, 264, 9798, 374, 264, 9155, 11, 1424, 1786, 11433, 480, 6573, 13, 68031, 525, 1865, 315, 9155, 26210, 11, 323, 26210, 646, 387, 1483, 803, 6707, 304, 3738, 7488, 1075, 21244, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.331, -0.0, -0.0847, -0.4301, -0.021, -0.0086, -0.0372, -0.8696, -0.0789, -0.0, -0.0014, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0052, -0.2022, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.4732, -0.0625, -0.4914, -0.0, -0.0325, -0.016, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0502, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0182, -0.0, -0.3889, -0.0, -0.0015, -0.0, -0.011, -0.0053, -0.0022, -0.0, -0.0032, -0.2014, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0015, -0.2834, -0.1602, -0.0002, -0.0127, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.1271, -0.4746, -0.0032, -0.459, -0.0036, -0.0, -0.1222, -0.0, -0.0, -0.8713, -0.0602, -0.2928, -0.0, -0.8273, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0037, -0.0235, -0.0018, -0.0299, -0.0, -0.0, -0.145, -0.067, -0.0023, -0.7364, -0.157, -0.0309, -0.0021, -0.0908, -0.00