{"id": "375", "pred": "DMSO is used for a variety of industrial and medical purposes. Industrially, it serves as an antifreeze and a solvent for many chemicals. Medically, it relieves pain, reduces swelling and inflammation, and promotes healing. It is applied to the skin for muscle and joint pain relief, burns, minor cuts, soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and conditions like scleroderma. Its ability to penetrate skin and tissue allows it to enter the bloodstream effectively, supporting its wide range of therapeutic uses.", "raw_output": "DMSO is used for a variety of industrial and medical purposes. Industrially, it serves as an antifreeze and a solvent for many chemicals. Medically, it relieves pain, reduces swelling and inflammation, and promotes healing. It is applied to the skin for muscle and joint pain relief, burns, minor cuts, soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and conditions like scleroderma. Its ability to penetrate skin and tissue allows it to enter the bloodstream effectively, supporting its wide range of therapeutic uses.", "gt": "DMSO, or dimethyl sulfoxide, is used in a variety of ways both industrially and medically. Industrially, it is used as an antifreeze and a solvent for numerous chemicals. Medically, DMSO is applied to the skin as an anti-inflammatory and general pain reliever, most commonly for muscles and joints. It is also used to promote healing for minor cuts, burns, soft tissue damage, local tissue death, and skin ulcers. DMSO has the unique ability to penetrate skin and tissue, allowing it to enter the bloodstream.", "question": "what is dmso used for", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 37.838, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [35, 4826, 46, 374, 1483, 369, 264, 8045, 315, 12785, 323, 6457, 9895, 13, 17210, 461, 745, 11, 432, 17045, 438, 458, 3196, 333, 27633, 32