{"id": "380", "pred": "DMSO is used for a variety of industrial and medical purposes. Industrially, it serves as an antifreeze and a solvent for many chemicals. Medically, it relieves pain, reduces swelling and inflammation, and promotes healing. It is applied to the skin for muscle and joint pain relief, burns, minor cuts, soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and conditions like scleroderma. Its ability to penetrate skin and tissue allows it to enter the bloodstream effectively, supporting its wide range of therapeutic uses.", "raw_output": "DMSO is used for a variety of industrial and medical purposes. Industrially, it serves as an antifreeze and a solvent for many chemicals. Medically, it relieves pain, reduces swelling and inflammation, and promotes healing. It is applied to the skin for muscle and joint pain relief, burns, minor cuts, soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and conditions like scleroderma. Its ability to penetrate skin and tissue allows it to enter the bloodstream effectively, supporting its wide range of therapeutic uses.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, DMSO is used for various purposes, including:\n\n1. Industrial uses: As an antifreeze and solvent for a wide range of chemicals.\n2. Medical uses: To relieve pain, reduce swelling and inflammation, promote healing, and treat a variety of medical ailments such as burns, scleroderma, and soft tissue damage.\n3. Pain relief: For muscles and joints, and as a general pain reliever applied to the skin.\n4. Skin care: To penetrate skin and tissue and enter the bloodstream.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What is DMSO used for?\" can be summarized as: DMSO is used for various industrial, medical, and personal care purposes, including pain relief, wound healing, and skin care.", "question": "what is dmso used for", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec