{"id": "381", "pred": "After completing these steps, the data in the selected column will be sorted alphabetically.", "raw_output": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\n\n1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings to select all cells in the worksheet.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name (e.g., the Product column).\n5. Choose alphabetical order (A to Z) for sorting.\n6. Click on the OK button.\n\nAfter completing these steps, the data in the selected column will be sorted alphabetically.", "gt": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, first click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. Then, switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. Click on the Sort option. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data. Alternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool to sort all worksheets.", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 42.535, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 8427, 2009, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 311, 3293, 678, 7761, 304, 279, 36636, 624, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 15967, 609, 12339, 1874, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 2999, 624, 19, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 3216, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 279, 5643, 3250, 4292, 20, 13, 22201, 83298, 1