{"id": "382", "pred": "After completing these steps, the data in the selected column will be sorted alphabetically.", "raw_output": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\n\n1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings to select all cells in the worksheet.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name (e.g., the Product column).\n5. Choose alphabetical order (A to Z) for sorting.\n6. Click on the OK button.\n\nAfter completing these steps, the data in the selected column will be sorted alphabetically.", "gt": "Passage 3 provides the necessary information to answer the question. To arrange an excel sheet alphabetically, click on the Select All button, switch to the Data tab, locate the Sort & Filter group, click on the Sort option, and then select the desired column to sort by.", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 42.702, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 8427, 2009, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 311, 3293, 678, 7761, 304, 279, 36636, 624, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 15967, 609, 12339, 1874, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 2999, 624, 19, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 3216, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 279, 5643, 3250, 4292, 20, 13, 22201, 83298, 1973, 320, 32, 311, 1863, 8, 369, 28273, 624, 21, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 10402, 3137, 382, 6025, 26568, 1493, 7354, 11, 279, 821, 304, 279, 4091, 3250, 686, 387, 10615, 27790, 2673, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0