{"id": "383", "pred": "After completing these steps, the data in the selected column will be sorted alphabetically.", "raw_output": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\n\n1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings to select all cells in the worksheet.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name (e.g., the Product column).\n5. Choose alphabetical order (A to Z) for sorting.\n6. Click on the OK button.\n\nAfter completing these steps, the data in the selected column will be sorted alphabetically.", "gt": "To arrange an excel sheet alphabetical, one can follow these steps:\n\n1. Select the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\n2. Click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu.\n3. When the Sort window appears, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\n4. Click on the OK button.\n5. The data should now be sorted in alphabetical order.", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 42.747, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 8427, 2009, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 311, 3293, 678, 7761, 304, 279, 36636, 624, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 15967, 609, 12339, 1874, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 2999, 624, 19, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 3216, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 279, 5643, 3250, 4292, 20, 13, 22201, 83298, 1973, 320, 