{"id": "408", "pred": "Push chunks or torn pieces of white bread through a food processor's shredding disk to", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passages, to make coarse bread crumbs similar to panko, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Push torn or chunked pieces of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet (or two half sheet pans in passage 3).\n4. Bake for 6 to 8 minutes (or about 5 minutes in passage 3) until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, or until they just begin to brown and become crisp.\n5. Shake the sheet(s) twice during baking to ensure even drying or browning.\n6. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\n7. Store in an airtight container at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\n\nNote: The method described in the passages makes coarse, oven-dried bread crumbs, which are similar in texture to panko but may not be identical to commercially produced panko, which is typically made from crustless bread and undergoes a specific pressing process. However, these homemade crumbs serve a similar culinary purpose.\n\nAnswer: Push chunks or torn pieces of white bread through a food processor's shredding disk to", "gt": "To make panko crumbs, preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C). Push torn pieces or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 degrees F for 6 to 8 minutes, shaking the sheet twice during baking. Remove from the oven and cool completely.", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 83.543, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 49247, 16002, 96577, 4428, 311, 281, 92852, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447,