{"id": "410", "pred": "Push chunks or torn pieces of white bread through a food processor's shredding disk to", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passages, to make coarse bread crumbs similar to panko, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Push torn or chunked pieces of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet (or two half sheet pans in passage 3).\n4. Bake for 6 to 8 minutes (or about 5 minutes in passage 3) until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, or until they just begin to brown and become crisp.\n5. Shake the sheet(s) twice during baking to ensure even drying or browning.\n6. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\n7. Store in an airtight container at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\n\nNote: The method described in the passages makes coarse, oven-dried bread crumbs, which are similar in texture to panko but may not be identical to commercially produced panko, which is typically made from crustless bread and undergoes a specific pressing process. However, these homemade crumbs serve a similar culinary purpose.\n\nAnswer: Push chunks or torn pieces of white bread through a food processor's shredding disk to", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Torn pieces of bread are pushed through the shredding disk of a food processor to create coarse crumbs.\n3. The crumbs are spread on a baking sheet.\n4. The sheet is baked in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes.\n5. The sheet is shaken twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n6. After baking, the crumbs are removed from the oven and allowed to cool completely.\n\nAlternatively, according to passage 2, you can also make panko crumbs by:\n\n1. Pushing chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to create coarse crumbs.\n2. Spreading the crumbs on a baking sheet and baking at 300 degrees F until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes.\n3. Shaking the sheet twice during baking.\n4. Being careful not to let the crumbs brown.\n\nFinally, passage 3 provides a third method for making panko crumbs, which involves blending the ingredients in a blender carafe and baking them on half sheet pans until they are crisp and lightly browned.", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 83.4, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 49247, 16002, 96577, 4428, 311, 281, 92852, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 22950, 21145, 476, 11879, 291, 9666, 315, 4158, 16002, 1526, 279, 52362, 287, 13364, 315, 264, 3607, 17654, 311, 1281, 49247, 96577, 624, 18, 13, 47716, 279, 96577, 41047, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 320, 269, 1378, 4279, 10834, 63783, 304, 21085, 220, 18, 4292, 19, 13, 52074, 369, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 4420, 320, 269, 911, 220, 20, 4420, 304, 21085, 220, 18, 8, 3080, 279, 96577, 525, 9058, 714, 537, 92872, 11, 476, 3080, 807, 1101, 3161, 311, 13876, 323, 3635, 41854, 624, 20, 13, 72323, 279, 10834, 1141, 8, 10917, 2337, 27815, 311, 5978, 1496, 45379, 476, 293, 50420, 624, 21, 13, 10783, 504, 279, 23387, 323, 7010, 6587, 624, 22, 13, 9129, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 518, 3054, 9315, 369, 705, 311, 220, 17, 5555, 382, 9112, 25, 576, 1714, 7481, 304, 279, 46769, 3643, 49247, 11, 23387, 1737, 4487, 16002, 96577, 11, 892, 525, 4428, 304, 10434, 311, 281, 92852, 714, 1231, 537, 387, 19516, 311, 53353, 8947, 281, 92852, 11, 892, 374, 11136, 1865, 504, 39612, 1717, 16002, 323, 36671, 288, 264, 3151, 25352, 1882, 13, 4354, 11, 1493, 35333, 96577, 8683, 264, 4428, 57341, 7428,