{"id": "411", "pred": "Push chunks or torn pieces of white bread through a food processor's shredding disk to", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passages, to make coarse bread crumbs similar to panko, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Push torn or chunked pieces of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet (or two half sheet pans in passage 3).\n4. Bake for 6 to 8 minutes (or about 5 minutes in passage 3) until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, or until they just begin to brown and become crisp.\n5. Shake the sheet(s) twice during baking to ensure even drying or browning.\n6. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\n7. Store in an airtight container at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\n\nNote: The method described in the passages makes coarse, oven-dried bread crumbs, which are similar in texture to panko but may not be identical to commercially produced panko, which is typically made from crustless bread and undergoes a specific pressing process. However, these homemade crumbs serve a similar culinary purpose.\n\nAnswer: Push chunks or torn pieces of white bread through a food processor's shredding disk to", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Push torn pieces of bread or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake in preheated oven until crumbs are dry but not toasted, 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs.\n5. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\n\nIf you want to store the panko crumbs for later use, you can transfer them to an airtight container and keep them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 83.323, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 49247, 16002, 96577, 4428, 311, 281, 92852, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 22950, 21145, 476, 11879, 291, 9666, 315, 4158, 16002, 1526, 279, 52362, 287, 13364, 315, 264, 3607, 17654, 311, 1281, 49247, 96577, 624, 18, 13, 47716, 279, 96577, 41047, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 320, 269, 1378, 4279, 10834, 63783, 304, 21085, 220, 18, 4292, 19, 13, 52074, 369, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 4420, 320, 269, 911, 220, 20, 4420, 304, 21085, 220, 18, 8, 3080, 279, 96577, 525, 9058, 714, 537, 92872, 11, 476, 3080, 807, 1101, 3161, 311, 13876, 323, 3635, 41854, 624, 20, 13, 72323, 279, 10834, 1141, 8, 10917, 2337, 27815, 311, 5978, 1496, 45379, 476, 293, 50420, 624, 21, 13, 10783, 504, 279, 23387, 323, 7010, 6587, 624, 22, 13, 9129, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 518, 3054, 9315, 369, 705, 311, 220, 17, 5555, 382, 9112, 25, 576, 1714, 7481, 304, 279, 46769, 3643, 49247, 11, 23387, 1737, 4487, 16002, 96577, 11, 892, 525, 4428, 304, 10434, 311, 281, 92852, 714, 1231, 537, 387, 19516, 311, 53353, 8947, 281, 92852, 11, 892, 374, 11136, 1865, 504, 39612, 1717, 16002, 323, 36671, 288, 264, 3151, 25352, 1882, 13, 4354, 11, 1493, 35333, 96577, 8683, 264, 4428, 57341, 7428, 382, 16141, 25, 22950, 26757, 476, 21145, 9666, 315, 4158, 16002, 1526, 264, 3607, 17654, 594, 52362, 287, 13364, 311], "logp_list": [-0.2468, -0.0002, -0.2288, -0.2672, -0.0183, -0.0166, -0.8536, -0.0002, -0.1172, -0.553, -0.0, -0.0495, -0.0789, -0.0036, 0.0, -0.8415, -0.1632, -0.001, -0.0791, -0.0096, -0.0091, -0.0, -0.6763, -0.0, -0.212, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0009, -0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.387, -0.0337