{"id": "423", "pred": "A UPC, or Universal Product Code, is a barcode symbology widely used in countries such as the United States, Canada, the United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and European nations to track trade items in stores. Specifically, UPC-A consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. Along with the related EAN barcode, it is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale according to GS1 specifications.", "raw_output": "A UPC, or Universal Product Code, is a barcode symbology widely used in countries such as the United States, Canada, the United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and European nations to track trade items in stores. Specifically, UPC-A consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. Along with the related EAN barcode, it is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale according to GS1 specifications.", "gt": "A UPC description refers to the Universal Product Code, which is a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item and is mainly used for scanning items at the point of sale.", "question": "what is a upc description", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 31.61, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [32, 95129, 11, 476, 25500, 5643, 6119, 11, 374, 264, 49407, 66654, 2449, 13570, 1483, 304, 5837, 1741, 438, 279, 3639, 4180, 11, 6864, 11, 279, 3639, 15072, 11, 8330, 11, 1532, 16911, 11, 323, 7513, 16675, 311, 3754, 6559, 3589, 304, 10533, 13, 44763, 11, 95129, 6691, 17167, 315, 220, 16, 17, 24064, 18509, 429, 525, 41229, 12607, 311, 1817, 6559, 1509, 13, 31844, 448, 279, 5435, 468, 1093, 49407, 11, 432, 374, 15503, 1483, 369, 35101, 6559, 3589, 518, 279, 1459, 315, 6278, 4092, 311, 35270, 16, 28703, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-