{"id": "425", "pred": "A UPC, or Universal Product Code, is a barcode symbology widely used in countries such as the United States, Canada, the United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and European nations to track trade items in stores. Specifically, UPC-A consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. Along with the related EAN barcode, it is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale according to GS1 specifications.", "raw_output": "A UPC, or Universal Product Code, is a barcode symbology widely used in countries such as the United States, Canada, the United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and European nations to track trade items in stores. Specifically, UPC-A consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. Along with the related EAN barcode, it is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale according to GS1 specifications.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, an UPDescription is:\n\n1. A barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores, consisting of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. (Passage 1)\n2. A process involving receiving a specimen bottle from a member, ensuring it contains a minimum of 30 milliliters of urine, initialing the label in the member's presence, and verifying the information on the label and DD Form 2624 (a military form). (Passage 2)\n3. A barcode partner that provides GS1 Originated UPC and EAN codes, as well as a toll-free number and positive customer reviews. (Passage 3)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "question": "what is a upc description", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 31.695, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [32, 95129, 11, 476, 25500, 5643, 6119, 11, 374, 264, 49407, 66654, 2449, 13570, 1483, 304, 5837, 1741, 438, 279, 3639, 4180, 11, 6864, 1