{"id": "433", "pred": "Use warm soapy water and a soft cloth for mild tarnish; for heavier tarnish, apply a baking soda paste with a lint-free cloth; alternatively, try a saltwater bath for lightly", "raw_output": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, the method depends on the severity of the tarnish and the type of jewelry:\n\nFor lightly tarnished silver: Use a salt bath by pouring two cups of hot water into a bowl (enough to cover the jewelry). This gentle cleanser removes tarnish without abrasion. For just one piece, use less water; for multiple pieces, use more. However, if the jewelry has gemstones, ensure they won't be affected by submersion in a saltwater solution.\n\nFor heavier tarnish on silver: Create a paste using three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the silver and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth (avoid paper towels, as they can scratch).\n\nFor dull or filmy silver: Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water, dip a soft cloth, rub the jewelry, rinse in cool water, and buff dry with a cloth.\n\nFor diamonds: Clean with warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush, then pat dry with a soft cloth.\n\nAnswer: Use warm soapy water and a soft cloth for mild tarnish; for heavier tarnish, apply a baking soda paste with a lint-free cloth; alternatively, try a saltwater bath for lightly", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to clean tarnished jewelry at home:\n\n1. Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip a soft cloth to shine silver jewelry that is merely dull or starting to discolor. Rub the jewelry, then rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry.\n2. Use warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush to clean diamonds. Pat the jewelry dry with a soft cloth.\n3. Soak tarnished silver jewelry in a saltwater solution of two cups of hot water. This method is gentle and can remove tarnish without abrading the silver. Make sure the gemstones will not be affected by the solution before submerging them.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide information on how to clean other types of jewelry, such as gold or platinum, or what to do if the tarnish is heavy or if the jewelry has intricate designs that may be damaged during cleaning.", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 82.425, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4240, 86480, 3304, 30717, 518, 2114, 11, 279, 1714, 13798, 389, 279, 29920, 315, 279, 86480, 812, 323, 279, 943, 315, 30717, 1447, 2461, 33404, 86480, 3304, 14961, 25, 5443, 264, 12021, 8885, 553, 50413, 1378, 25374, 315, 4017, 3015, 1119, 264, 19212, 320, 268, 1384, 311, 3421, 279, 30717, 568, 1096, 21700, 34194, 261, 28160, 86480, 812, 2041, 58581, 290, 13, 1752, 1101, 825, 6573, 11, 990, 2686, 3015, 26, 369, 5248, 9666, 11, 990, 803, 13, 4354, 11, 421, 279, 30717, 702, 18747, 32510, 11, 5978, 807, 2765, 944, 387, 11495, 553, 1186, 76, 1325, 304, 264, 12021, 12987, 6291, 382, 2461, 43822, 86480, 812, 389, 14961, 25, 4230, 264, 24937, 1667, 2326, 5479, 27815, 38862, 311, 825, 949, 3015, 13, 44856, 279, 14961, 323, 3796, 279, 31881, 448, 264, 8413, 11, 57920, 12577, 27292, 320, 47856, 5567, 52884, 11, 438, 807, 646, 18778, 3593, 2461, 40530, 476, 89394, 14961, 25, 19219, 264, 2421, 21025, 315, 23034, 12000, 26785, 448, 8205, 3015, 11, 23604, 264, 8413, 27292, 11, 10273, 279, 30717, 11, 73241, 304, 7010, 3015, 11, 323, 11522, 9058, 448, 264, 27292, 382, 2461, 48051, 25, 9590, 448, 8205, 773, 9667, 3015, 323, 264, 8413, 30117, 28300, 15625, 476, 2310, 25507, 36061, 11, 1221, 3272, 9058, 448, 264, 8413, 27292, 382, 16141, 25, 5443, 8205, 773, 9667, 3015, 323, 264, 8413, 27292, 369, 23034, 86480, 812, 26, 369, 43822, 86480, 812, 11, 3796, 264, 27815, 38862, 24937, 448, 264, 57920, 12577, 27292,