{"id": "436", "pred": "Tip: Knowing the person's middle name can be very helpful to ensure you are identifying the correct individual, especially", "raw_output": "To find someone in France, you can use the following methods as described in the passages:\n\n1. Use a people search website for France to locate relatives by sending an email or letter to the town hall in the city of their birth if you know where they were born.\n\n2. Try the French white pages in English at http://www.pagesjaunes.fr/pb.cgi?lang=en. Instead of typing Paris in the City field, enter IDF (or Ile de France) in the Dept district or region field to search Paris and its suburbs.\n\n3. Visit www.pagesjaunes.fr (Pages Blanches), the French version of the white pages:\n   - Enter the last name in the Nom field.\n   - Optionally, enter the first name in Prenom.\n   - Input address information in the Ou section if known; otherwise, leave it blank to search the entire country.\n   - Click Trouver to search for the name. The results will display name, address, and phone number for all matching listings.\n\nAdditionally, posting a missed connection (MC) on Paris Craigslist (http://paris.craigslist.org/cgi-bin/pers...) may also help.\n\nTip: Knowing the person's middle name can be very helpful to ensure you are identifying the correct individual, especially", "gt": "To find someone in France, you can use the website www.pagesjaunes.fr, the French version of the white pages. Enter the last name of the person in the \"Nom\" field and optionally enter their first name in the \"Prenom\" field. If you know the address, you can enter it in the \"Ou\" section. Leave it blank if you don't know the address. Click on \"Trouver\" to search for the name. The search results will display the name, address, and phone number of the matching listings.", "question": "how to find someone in france", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": 