{"id": "471", "pred": "4. Taste: Unrefined coconut oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma, while refined coconut oil lacks any noticeable taste or smell.", "raw_output": "The differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil include:\n\n1. Source: Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil (also called pure or virgin coconut oil) is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts.\n\n2. Aroma and flavor: Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil is deodorized and has no discernible taste or smell.\n\n3. Smoking point: Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450°F, compared to unrefined coconut oil, which has a smoking point of 350°F. This makes refined coconut oil more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.\n\n4. Taste: Unrefined coconut oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma, while refined coconut oil lacks any noticeable taste or smell.", "gt": "Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, has no discernible taste or smell, and has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking. On the other hand, unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma, and has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F.", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 60.112, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 11799, 1948, 37191, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 8748, 25, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 31620, 33457, 13779, 11, 1393, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 320, 18654, 2598, 10526, 476, 35899, 33457, 5590, 8, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 24955, 315, 7722, 1062, 443, 6128, 382, 17, 13, 362, 56984, 323, 1717