{"id": "473", "pred": "4. Taste: Unrefined coconut oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma, while refined coconut oil lacks any noticeable taste or smell.", "raw_output": "The differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil include:\n\n1. Source: Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil (also called pure or virgin coconut oil) is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts.\n\n2. Aroma and flavor: Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil is deodorized and has no discernible taste or smell.\n\n3. Smoking point: Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450°F, compared to unrefined coconut oil, which has a smoking point of 350°F. This makes refined coconut oil more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.\n\n4. Taste: Unrefined coconut oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma, while refined coconut oil lacks any noticeable taste or smell.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil is the process used to extract it. Refined coconut oil is extracted from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is extracted from the flesh of the fresh coconut. Another difference is that refined coconut oil has a higher smoke point and is therefore better suited for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized and has no taste or smell, while unrefined oil retains its distinctive coconut flavor and aroma.", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 60.287, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 11799, 1948, 37191, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 8748, 25, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 374, 186