{"id": "474", "pred": "4. Taste: Unrefined coconut oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma, while refined coconut oil lacks any noticeable taste or smell.", "raw_output": "The differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil include:\n\n1. Source: Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil (also called pure or virgin coconut oil) is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts.\n\n2. Aroma and flavor: Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil is deodorized and has no discernible taste or smell.\n\n3. Smoking point: Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450°F, compared to unrefined coconut oil, which has a smoking point of 350°F. This makes refined coconut oil more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.\n\n4. Taste: Unrefined coconut oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma, while refined coconut oil lacks any noticeable taste or smell.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are:\n\n1. Source: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts.\n2. Aroma and flavor: Unrefined coconut oil retains its distinct aroma and flavor, while refined coconut oil loses these qualities during the refining process.\n3. Smoking point: Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point (450 degrees F) than unrefined coconut oil (350 degrees F), making it more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.\n\nTherefore, the main differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are their source, aroma, flavor, and smoking point.", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 59.894, "status": "success", "