{"id": "478", "pred": "Additionally, this service allows you to notify up to 100 organizations besides USPS and uses encryption technologies to secure your data. It is useful for both personal permanent moves/temporary relocations and for businesses, especially after disasters requiring relocation.", "raw_output": "You can change your U.S. Postal Service address in as little as 1 minute using the online service. There are three ways to do this:  \n1. Visit https://moversguide.usps.com/, where identity validation is done with a $1 charge to your credit or debit card.  \n2. Call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777).  \n3. Fill out and submit PS Form 3575 either in person at any U.S. Post Office, by mail to any Post Office, or directly to a Postal Mail Carrier.  \n\nAdditionally, this service allows you to notify up to 100 organizations besides USPS and uses encryption technologies to secure your data. It is useful for both personal permanent moves/temporary relocations and for businesses, especially after disasters requiring relocation.", "gt": "Passage 3 provides information on how to change your address with the U.S. Postal Service. You can visit their website, call the USPS Call Center, or fill out and submit a form at a U.S. Post Office.", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 60.2, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [2610, 646, 2297, 697, 547, 808, 13, 54217, 5362, 2621, 304, 438, 2632, 438, 220, 16, 9383, 1667, 279, 2860, 2473, 13, 2619, 525, 2326, 5510, 311, 653, 419, 25, 2303, 16, 13, 19008, 3703, 1110, 76, 8969, 48370, 21916, 1690, 905, 34545, 1380, 9569, 10519, 374, 2814, 448, 264, 400, 16, 6757, 311, 697, 6668, 476, 45353, 3701, 13, 2303, 17, 13, 7143, 279, 84876, 7143, 5832, 518, 220, 16, 12, 23, 15, 15, 12, 7384, 32340, 5012, 320, 16, 12, 23, 15, 15, 12,