{"id": "479", "pred": "Additionally, this service allows you to notify up to 100 organizations besides USPS and uses encryption technologies to secure your data. It is useful for both personal permanent moves/temporary relocations and for businesses, especially after disasters requiring relocation.", "raw_output": "You can change your U.S. Postal Service address in as little as 1 minute using the online service. There are three ways to do this:  \n1. Visit https://moversguide.usps.com/, where identity validation is done with a $1 charge to your credit or debit card.  \n2. Call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777).  \n3. Fill out and submit PS Form 3575 either in person at any U.S. Post Office, by mail to any Post Office, or directly to a Postal Mail Carrier.  \n\nAdditionally, this service allows you to notify up to 100 organizations besides USPS and uses encryption technologies to secure your data. It is useful for both personal permanent moves/temporary relocations and for businesses, especially after disasters requiring relocation.", "gt": "To change your US postal address, you can visit the official website of the U.S. Postal Service, fill out an online form, or contact their call center. The process is fast and versatile, allowing you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the USPS. It's important to note that you can also use this feature to have your business mail forwarded to a new address due to a permanent move or temporary relocation. The process involves submitting either an online form or filling out and submitting a physical form at any U.S. Post Office.", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 60.149, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [2610, 646, 2297, 697, 547, 808, 13, 54217, 5362, 2621, 304, 438, 2632, 438, 220, 16, 9383, 1667, 279, 2860