{"id": "489", "pred": "You can track who favorited your tweets by using websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These platforms allow you to see which users have favorited your tweets or have favorited the same tweets as you. Additionally, you can set up your Twitter account to receive email notifications whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite by going to your Twitter Settings, clicking on the blue Notifications link, and configuring your notification preferences.", "raw_output": "You can track who favorited your tweets by using websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These platforms allow you to see which users have favorited your tweets or have favorited the same tweets as you. Additionally, you can set up your Twitter account to receive email notifications whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite by going to your Twitter Settings, clicking on the blue Notifications link, and configuring your notification preferences.", "gt": "You can see who liked your tweets by using tracking websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These sites can give you an idea of who is favouriting your tweets. Alternatively, you can also set up notifications on Twitter itself. By going to your account settings and clicking on the notifications link, you can arrange to be notified via email whenever someone likes one of your tweets.", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 30.708, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [2610, 646, 3754, 879, 4694, 1608, 697, 23150, 553, 1667, 13037, 1741, 438, 80941, 354, 465, 5071, 323, 80941, 11870, 70485, 13, 4220, 15409, 2138, 498, 311, 1490, 892, 3847, 614, 4694, 1608, 697, 23150, 476, 614, 4694, 1608, 279, 1852, 23150, 438, 498, 13, 22406, 11, 498, 646, 738, 705, 697, 6271, 2692, 311, 5258, 2551, 21969, 15356, 4325, 15423, 82