{"id": "492", "pred": "You can track who favorited your tweets by using websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These platforms allow you to see which users have favorited your tweets or have favorited the same tweets as you. Additionally, you can set up your Twitter account to receive email notifications whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite by going to your Twitter Settings, clicking on the blue Notifications link, and configuring your notification preferences.", "raw_output": "You can track who favorited your tweets by using websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These platforms allow you to see which users have favorited your tweets or have favorited the same tweets as you. Additionally, you can set up your Twitter account to receive email notifications whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite by going to your Twitter Settings, clicking on the blue Notifications link, and configuring your notification preferences.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, there are several ways to track who likes your tweets:\n\n1. Favotter.net and Favstar.fm - These websites allow you to track who has favorited your tweets and which tweets have been favorited by multiple users. (Passage 1)\n2. Using a web-based website - There are websites that allow you to check Twitter users who favorite tweets. (Passage 2)\n3. On Twitter - You can set up your account settings to receive notifications via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is: You can use Favotter.net, Favstar.fm, or a web-based website to track who likes your tweets, or you can set up your Twitter account settings to receive email notifications.", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 30.614, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "tok