{"id": "504", "pred": "The tropical rainforest floor is home to herbs and mushrooms that grow on it. Due to the heat and moisture in the biome, dead plants and animals rot quickly, providing rich nutrients that support the growth of other plants. Vines and ferns also grow throughout the biome, connecting its various layers, including the forest floor. Bananas grow on vines within this biome as well.", "raw_output": "The tropical rainforest floor is home to herbs and mushrooms that grow on it. Due to the heat and moisture in the biome, dead plants and animals rot quickly, providing rich nutrients that support the growth of other plants. Vines and ferns also grow throughout the biome, connecting its various layers, including the forest floor. Bananas grow on vines within this biome as well.", "gt": "The floor of a tropical rainforest biome is characterized by a fast rate of decay due to the heat and moisture. This decay provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow. Various types of fruits, nuts, herbs, and mushrooms grow on the rainforest floor. Additionally, vines and ferns grow all over the rainforest, including the floor, helping to connect the various layers of the biome.", "question": "what are the characteristics of tropical rainforest floor", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 26.979, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 374, 2114, 311, 41293, 323, 47151, 429, 3063, 389, 432, 13, 23662, 311, 279, 8628, 323, 31157, 304, 279, 83610, 11, 5593, 10779, 323, 9898, 5749, 6157, 11, 8241, 9080, 36393, 429, 1824, 279, 6513, 315, 1008, 10779, 13, 647, 1543, 323, 87024, 82, 1083, 3063, 6814, 279, 83610, 11, 20913, 1181, 5257, 13617, 11, 2670, 279, 13638, 6422, 13, 22730, 25908, 3063, 389, 85429, 2878, 419, 83610, 438, 1632, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.5023, -0.2826, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1737, -0.3498, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0004, 0.0, -0.5267, -0.0, -0.5813, -0.0182, -0.0303, -0.0336, 0.0, -0.0003, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.4087, -0.0298, -0.0044, -0.0, -0.3745, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0082, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.4957, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.2015, -0.0385, -0.0477, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0112, -0.0004, -0.0028, -0.54, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.057, -0.1378, -0.1546, -0.0009, -0.1209, -0.6932, -0.5981, -0.7341, -0.0111, -0.0, -0.0595, -0.3392, -0.0106, -0.4742, -0.0, -0.0017, -0.2193, -0.0, -0.1301, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.7725, -0.0789, -0.3966, -0.4128, -0.0048, -0.0859, -0.1859], "cumulative_logprob": -10.3446, "norm_logp": -0.1343, "input_len": 487, "output_tokens": 77, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.42, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "507", "pred": "The tropical rainforest floor is home to herbs and mushrooms that grow on it. Due to the heat and moisture in the biome, dead plants and animals rot quickly, providing rich nutrients that support the growth of other plants. Vines and ferns also grow throughout the biome, connecting its various layers, including the forest floor. Bananas grow on vines within this biome as well.", "raw_output": "The tropical rainforest floor is home to herbs and mushrooms that grow on it. Due to the heat and moisture in the biome, dead plants and animals rot quickly, providing rich nutrients that support the growth of other plants. Vines and ferns also grow throughout the biome, connecting its various layers, including the forest floor. Bananas grow on vines within this biome as well.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor are:\n\n1. High levels of rainfall, with some areas receiving up to 400 inches of rain annually.\n2. High humidity due to the large amount of rainfall.\n3. Abundant vegetation, including tall trees, vines, ferns, herbs, mushrooms, fruits, and nuts.\n4. Quick decay of plant and animal matter due to the heat and moisture, which provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow.\n5. Presence of bananas growing on vines.\n\nTherefore, the tropical rainforest floor is characterized by high rainfall, humidity, and lush vegetation, with a diverse array of plant species and a rapid rate of decay and nutrient cycling.", "question": "what are the characteristics of tropical rainforest floor", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 26.947, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 374, 2114, 311, 41293, 323, 47151, 429, 3063, 389, 432, 13, 23662, 311, 279, 8628, 323, 31157, 304, 279, 83610, 11, 5593, 10779, 323, 9898, 5749, 6157, 11, 8241, 9080, 36393, 429, 1824, 279, 6513, 315, 1008, 10779, 13, 647, 1543, 323, 87024, 82, 1083, 3063, 6814, 279, 83610, 11, 20913, 1181, 5257, 13617, 11, 2670, 279, 13638, 6422, 13, 22730, 25908, 3063, 389, 85429, 2878, 419, 83610, 438, 1632, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.5023, -0.2826, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1737, -0.3498, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0004, 0.0, -0.5267, -0.0, -0.5813, -0.0182, -0.0303, -0.0336, 0.0, -0.0003, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.4087, -0.0298, -0.0044, -0.0, -0.3745, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0082, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.4957, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.2015, -0.0385, -0.0477, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0112, -0.0004, -0.0028, -0.54, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.057, -0.1378, -0.1546, -0.0009, -0.1209, -0.6932, -0.5981, -0.7341, -0.0111, -0.0, -0.0595, -0.3392, -0.0106, -0.4742, -0.0, -0.0017, -0.2193, -0.0, -0.1301, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.7725, -0.0789, -0.3966, -0.4128, -0.0048, -0.0859, -0.1859], "cumulative_logprob": -10.3446, "norm_logp": -0.1343, "input_len": 487, "output_tokens": 77, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 31.93, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "508", "pred": "The difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that sirloin steak is a broader category of steak cut from the back of the animal, specifically the rear back portion continuing off the short loin. In contrast, a porterhouse steak is a specific cut from the short loin area that includes a large portion of the tenderloin (fillet) on one side of a T-shaped bone and part of the strip steak (front of the sirloin) on the other. Additionally, porterhouse steaks contain more tenderloin than T-bone steaks and are generally larger and more expensive.", "raw_output": "The difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that sirloin steak is a broader category of steak cut from the back of the animal, specifically the rear back portion continuing off the short loin. In contrast, a porterhouse steak is a specific cut from the short loin area that includes a large portion of the tenderloin (fillet) on one side of a T-shaped bone and part of the strip steak (front of the sirloin) on the other. Additionally, porterhouse steaks contain more tenderloin than T-bone steaks and are generally larger and more expensive.", "gt": "Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and contain more of the tenderloin or fillet than sirloin steaks. They are essentially a larger version of the T-Bone steak, carved from a larger portion of the tenderloin. On the other hand, the sirloin steak is a steak cut from the back of the animal, continuing off the short loin from which T-bone, porterhouse, and club steaks are cut. The sirloin is divided into several different types of steak.", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 41.405, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 323, 87186, 7675, 48959, 3