{"id": "509", "pred": "The difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that sirloin steak is a broader category of steak cut from the back of the animal, specifically the rear back portion continuing off the short loin. In contrast, a porterhouse steak is a specific cut from the short loin area that includes a large portion of the tenderloin (fillet) on one side of a T-shaped bone and part of the strip steak (front of the sirloin) on the other. Additionally, porterhouse steaks contain more tenderloin than T-bone steaks and are generally larger and more expensive.", "raw_output": "The difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that sirloin steak is a broader category of steak cut from the back of the animal, specifically the rear back portion continuing off the short loin. In contrast, a porterhouse steak is a specific cut from the short loin area that includes a large portion of the tenderloin (fillet) on one side of a T-shaped bone and part of the strip steak (front of the sirloin) on the other. Additionally, porterhouse steaks contain more tenderloin than T-bone steaks and are generally larger and more expensive.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that porterhouse steak is a larger version of T-Bone steak and it contains more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steak.", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 41.427, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 323, 87186, 7675, 48959, 374, 429, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 374, 264, 26829, 5582, 315, 48959, 3931, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 9864, 11, 11689, 279, 14639, 1182, 13348, 14354, 1007, 279, 2805, 76960, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 264, 87186, 7675, 48959, 374, 264, 3151, 3931, 504, 