{"id": "510", "pred": "The difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that sirloin steak is a broader category of steak cut from the back of the animal, specifically the rear back portion continuing off the short loin. In contrast, a porterhouse steak is a specific cut from the short loin area that includes a large portion of the tenderloin (fillet) on one side of a T-shaped bone and part of the strip steak (front of the sirloin) on the other. Additionally, porterhouse steaks contain more tenderloin than T-bone steaks and are generally larger and more expensive.", "raw_output": "The difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that sirloin steak is a broader category of steak cut from the back of the animal, specifically the rear back portion continuing off the short loin. In contrast, a porterhouse steak is a specific cut from the short loin area that includes a large portion of the tenderloin (fillet) on one side of a T-shaped bone and part of the strip steak (front of the sirloin) on the other. Additionally, porterhouse steaks contain more tenderloin than T-bone steaks and are generally larger and more expensive.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it appears that the main difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is their location within the sirloin muscle. Sirloin steaks are cut from the back of the animal and continue off the short loin from which other cuts such as T-bone and porterhouse steaks are made. On the other hand, porterhouse steaks are specifically carved from the larger portion of the tenderloin and therefore have more of the tenderloin or fillet compared to T-bone steaks. However, the passages suggest that both sirloin and porterhouse steaks may be referred to as the same thing or as a large version of the T-bone due to their similarity in appearance and taste.", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 41.681, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 323, 87186, 7675, 48959, 374, 429, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 374, 264, 26829, 5582, 315, 48959, 3931, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 9864, 11, 11689, 279, 14639, 1182, 13348, 14354, 1007, 279, 2805, 76960, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 264, 87186, 7675, 48959, 374, 264, 3151, 3931, 504, 279, 2805, 76960, 3082, 429, 5646, 264, 3460, 13348, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 320, 12441, 1149, 8, 389, 825, 3108, 315, 264, 350, 34731, 17240, 323, 949, 315, 279, 13316, 48959, 320, 6951, 315, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 8, 389, 279, 1008, 13, 22406, 11, 87186, 7675, 4087, 9810, 6644, 803, 27582, 385, 258, 1091, 350, 1455, 603, 4087, 9810, 323, 525, 8789, 8131, 323, 803, 11392, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.271, -0.6203, -0.0242, -0.5874, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0098, -0.0, -0.1279, -0.0, -0.0, -0.3196, -0.0698, -0.5987, -0.0, 0.0, -0.4754, -0.0299, -0.2551, -0.5441, -0.1648, -0.6123, -0.1611, -0.0381, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1003, -0.2051, -0.0, -0.0025, -0.0067, -0.2431, -0.6955, -0.0001, -0.0025, -0.0, -0.0009, -0.0041, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0743, -0.2648, -0.0012, -0.0, -0.3244, -0.0346, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0116, -0.0112, -0.465, -1.0333, -0.0032, -0.0029, -0.0, -0.07, -0.1418, -0.0282, -0.2019, -0.6955, -0.016, -0.0, -0.0583, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0, -0.7173, -0.0243, -0.0, -0.0073, -0.7532, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0028, -0.0022, -0.4587, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0562, -0.2026, -0.0, -0.0, -0.4019, -0.3607, -0.2526, -1.1611, -0.0061, -0.0019, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0043, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.6715, -1.2949, -0.0, -0.4295, -0.0, -0.0037, -0.0, -0.2373, -0.0573, -0.2535, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1816, -0.0078, -0.1602, -0.0007, -0.0057, 0.0, -0.3105, -0.0246, -0.8699, -0.6304, -0.6556, -0.0671, -0.0173, -0.0632, -0.0329], "cumulative_logprob": -19.9983, "norm_logp": -0.1613, "input_len": 505, "output_tokens": 124, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.51, "GAVIE-