{"id": "518", "pred": "Raffles work by selling numbered tickets to participants, and winners are determined through a random drawing. In a reverse raffle, tickets are drawn one by one, and the last remaining ticket wins. In a 50-50 draw, tickets are sold during an event, and 50% of the proceeds go to a randomly selected winner while the other 50% supports a charitable cause. Some raffles, like cash tip board raffles, offer additional chances to win specific prizes beyond standard ticket entries.", "raw_output": "Raffles work by selling numbered tickets to participants, and winners are determined through a random drawing. In a reverse raffle, tickets are drawn one by one, and the last remaining ticket wins. In a 50-50 draw, tickets are sold during an event, and 50% of the proceeds go to a randomly selected winner while the other 50% supports a charitable cause. Some raffles, like cash tip board raffles, offer additional chances to win specific prizes beyond standard ticket entries.", "gt": "Raffles work by selling tickets to participants, who have the opportunity to win prizes. The specific details and mechanics of a raffle can vary. In a reverse raffle, participants purchase tickets with numbers on them, and the last ticket drawn wins the main prize. In a 50-50 draw, tickets are sold during an event, and 50% of the proceeds go to the winner of a random draw, while the other 50% is allocated for a charitable purpose. In some cases, raffles may also offer additional opportunities to win prizes, such as cash tip board raffles.", "question": "how do raffles work", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 35.847, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [49, 80535, 975, 553, 11236, 48826, 14403, 311, 13026, 11, 323, 25448, 525, 10838, 1526, 264, 4194, 13330, 13, 758, 264, 9931, 435, 44090, 11, 14403, 525, 14764, 825, 553, 825, 11, 323, 279, 1537, 96