{"id": "530", "pred": "E-ZPass charges work by reading the toll tag mounted on your vehicle's windshield as it enters the toll lane. The antennae detect the tag, and your E-ZPass® account is automatically charged the proper toll amount as your vehicle passes through. Feedback is provided on an electronic display. If your vehicle does not have a toll tag, it is classified as a violator, and cameras take photos of your license plate for processing and billing.", "raw_output": "E-ZPass charges work by reading the toll tag mounted on your vehicle's windshield as it enters the toll lane. The antennae detect the tag, and your E-ZPass® account is automatically charged the proper toll amount as your vehicle passes through. Feedback is provided on an electronic display. If your vehicle does not have a toll tag, it is classified as a violator, and cameras take photos of your license plate for processing and billing.", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here is how E-ZPass charging works:\n\nWhen you sign up for E-ZPass, a certain amount is charged to your credit card to establish a balance (specifically, $100 for the EZ-Tag and $25 for the TX-Tag). This balance is used to pay for tolls as you drive through toll lanes. When you drive through a toll booth, the toll tag mounted on your windshield is read by the antennae, and your E-ZPass account is charged the appropriate amount. The amount is deducted from your balance. If your balance falls below a certain threshold ($10 for the TX-Tag), E-ZPass will charge your credit card an additional $100 or $25 to top up your balance.", "question": "how does ez pass charges work", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 31.279, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [36, 11171, 12187, 10195, 975, 553, 5290, 279, 25851, 4772, 21810, 389, 697, 7310, 594, 73939, 438, 432, 28833, 279, 25851, 21272, 13, 576, 714