{"id": "592", "pred": "The information from Form 1099-PATR is reported on Schedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835, which are then included with Form 1040.", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passages, Form 1099-PATR reports taxable distributions received from cooperatives, and the IRS instructions state that patronage dividends and other distributions in boxes 1, 2, 3, and 5 should be reported on Schedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835. These schedules or forms are then included as part of the overall tax return, which is Form 1040. Therefore, Form 1099-PATR does not go directly on Form 1040; instead, the information from it is reported on Schedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835, which are attached to Form 1040.\n\nAnswer: The information from Form 1099-PATR is reported on Schedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835, which are then included with Form 1040.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the answer to the question \"Where does 1099-PATR go on 1040?\" is:\n\nSchedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835.\n\nAccording to the instructions for Form 1099-PATR, patronage dividends and other distributions in boxes 1, 2, 3, and 5 from a cooperative are reported on one of these forms.", "question": "where does 1099-patr go on 1040", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 62.497, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 3377, 220, 16, 15, 24, 24, 9299, 828, 49, 6682, 58353, 42685, 3949, 504, 21676, 5859, 11, 323, 279, 33383, 11221, 1584, 429, 35280, 424, 55264, 323, 1008, 42685, 304, 14697, 220, 16, 11, 220, 17, 11, 220, 18, 11, 323, 220, 20, 1265, 387, 4961, 389, 23512, 356, 11, 23512, 434, 11, 476, 3377, 220, 19, 23, 18, 20, 13, 4220, 36769, 476, 7586, 525, 1221, 5230, 438, 949, 315, 279, 8084, 3742, 470, 11, 892, 374, 3377, 220, 16, 15, 19, 15, 13, 15277, 11, 3377, 220, 16, 15, 24, 24, 9299, 828, 49, 1558, 537, 728, 5961, 389, 337