{"id": "601", "pred": "Cycling is a type of aerobic exercise that may be better than other forms of aerobic exercise for individuals with arthritic or orthopedic problems due to its low-impact nature.", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passages, cycling is a type of aerobic exercise. Passage 2 highlights that cycling has wide appeal and value and may be ideal for individuals with orthopedic issues like arthritis who cannot walk for long periods. Passage 3 notes that the stationary bike provides the lowest impact workout compared to equipment like treadmills and rowing machines because it supports most of the user's weight.\n\nSince cycling is a form of aerobic exercise and offers specific benefits such as low impact and suitability for people with joint problems, it can be considered a particularly beneficial aerobic activity for certain individuals. However, the passages do not compare all forms of aerobic exercise in general, nor do they state that cycling is universally better than all other aerobic exercises.\n\nTherefore, the answer depends on individual needs and conditions. For people with joint issues, cycling may be better than other aerobic exercises like running or walking. For others, different aerobic activities may be more suitable.\n\nAnswer: Cycling is a type of aerobic exercise that may be better than other forms of aerobic exercise for individuals with arthritic or orthopedic problems due to its low-impact nature.", "gt": "The passages suggest that both cycling and aerobic exercise are beneficial. However, cycling, including stationary cycling, may be particularly ideal for individuals with arthritic or other orthopedic problems who may have difficulty walking for extended periods. Furthermore, stationary biking provides a low impact workout as it supports the majority of your weight. Therefore, while both exercises are valuable, the passages may imply that cycling could be better for those with specific physical conditions.", "question": "which is better exercise cycling or aerobic", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 73.043, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 32062, 374, 264, 943, 315, 90390, 10158, 13, 98475, 220, 17, 21314, 429, 32062, 702, 6884, 14303, 323, 897, 323, 1231, 387, 10507, 369, 7775, 448, 29199, 16367, 292, 4714, 1075, 54552, 879, 4157, 4227, 369, 1293, 18346, 13, 98475, 220, 18, 8388, 429, 279, 52635, 12963, 5707, 279, 15457, 5421, 25242, 7707, 311, 7096, 1075, 47714, 76, 3305, 323, 2802, 287, 12645, 1576, 432, 11554, 1429, 315, 279, 1196, 594, 4680, 382, 12549, 32062, 374, 264, 1352, 315, 90390, 10158, 323, 6081, 3151, 7567, 1741, 438, 3347, 5421, 323, 80628, 369, 1251, 448, 10284, 5322, 11, 432, 646, 387, 6509, 264, 7945, 23699, 90390, 5702, 369, 3654, 7775, 13, 4354, 11, 279, 46769, 653, 537, 9429, 678, 7586, 315, 90390, 10158, 304, 4586, 11, 6329, 653, 807, 1584, 429, 32062, 374, 60428, 2664, 1091, 678, 1008, 90390, 22932, 382, 54815, 11, 279, 4226, 13798, 389, 3842, 3880, 323, 4682, 13, 1752, 1251, 448, 10284, 4714, 11, 32062, 1231, 387, 2664, 1091, 1008, 90390, 22932, 1075, 4303, 476, 11435, 13, 1752, 3800, 11, 2155, 90390, 7488, 1231, 387, 803, 14452, 382, 16141, 25, 59970, 374, 264, 943, 315, 90390, 10158, 429, 1231, 387, 2664, 1091, 1008, 7586, 315, 90390, 10158, 369, 7775, 448, 796, 339, 49208, 476, 29199, 16367, 292, 5322, 4152, 311, 1181, 3347, 12, 57300, 6993, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.25, -0.0001, -0.0762, -0.4533, -0.0105, -0.034, -0.0764, -0.0055, -0.7126, -0.2539, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.98, -0.0066, -0.0, -0.1129, -0.4291, -0.1162, -0.0155, -0.0669, -0.3146, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.6392, -0.0774, -0.0008, -0.0365, -0.0001, -0.0814, -0.3156, -0.7041, -0.0, 0.0, -0.2112, -0.6198, -0.0002, -0.1293, -0.1113, -0.0002, -0.056, -0.0801, -0.2449, -0.705, -0.01, 0.0, -0.0004, -0.4752, -0.0001, -0.3194, -0.2014,