{"id": "620", "pred": "Overall, technology has modernized the workplace by enhancing productivity, changing attitudes and processes, and enabling greater flexibility and global connectivity.", "raw_output": "Technology has changed the workplace in several significant ways as described across the passages:\n\n1. It has improved **efficiency and increased productivity**, altering how time is spent in the modern workplace.\n2. It has transformed the **dynamics of the workplace** and shifted business practices over the last 10 to 15 years.\n3. It has dramatically reshaped the average workplace in America, replacing the office environment of the past with rapid technological advancements.\n4. Employees can now interact with a **global market** and work remotely (\"take work out on the road\").\n\nOverall, technology has modernized the workplace by enhancing productivity, changing attitudes and processes, and enabling greater flexibility and global connectivity.", "gt": "IT technology has significantly changed the workplace in several ways. It has improved efficiency and increased productivity, as it allows for a complete shift in how time is spent in the modern workplace. The continuous evolution of technology also changes how business is conducted and the dynamics of the workplace. Over the last 10 to 15 years, technology has drastically changed attitudes and processes in the workplace. Technology has also dramatically reshaped the average American workplace, allowing employees to interact with a global market and take work on the road.", "question": "how has it technology changed the workplace", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 46.303, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [62407, 702, 5497, 279, 26368, 304, 3807, 5089, 5510, 438, 7481, 3941, 279, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 1084, 702, 12944, 3070, 6445, 10387, 323, 7172, 25148, 97219, 59823, 