{"id": "636", "pred": "Differences:\n- The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\n- Transmission in the nervous system occurs via electrochemical pulses, whereas the Endocrine System uses hormones (chemicals) for signal transmission.\n- The nervous system is continuous with interconnected cells, while the organs of the Endocrine System are discrete and not physically connected.\n- The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the Endocrine System relies on the circulatory system for signal transmission.", "raw_output": "Similarities:\n- Both the nervous system and the endocrine system are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n- Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\n- Chemical messengers are important in both systems, although their method of transmission and release differs.\n\nDifferences:\n- The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\n- Transmission in the nervous system occurs via electrochemical pulses, whereas the Endocrine System uses hormones (chemicals) for signal transmission.\n- The nervous system is continuous with interconnected cells, while the organs of the Endocrine System are discrete and not physically connected.\n- The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the Endocrine System relies on the circulatory system for signal transmission.", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here are the key differences and similarities between the nervous system and the endocrine system:\n\nDifferences:\n\n* The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n* Transmission in the nervous system occurs through electrochemical pulses, while in the endocrine system, it is done through chemicals called hormones.\n* The nervous system is continuous and interconnected, while the endocrine system consists of discrete organs.\n* The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system.\n\nSimilarities:\n\n* Both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n* Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\n* Chemical messengers are important in both systems, although their method of transmission and release differs.\n\nTherefore, based on the given passages, the nervous system and endocrine system have different structures and methods of transmission, but they share similar functions and regulatory mechanisms.", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 54.755, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 510, 12, 11733, 279, 22596, 1849, 323, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 315, 1008, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 624, 12, 11733, 5942, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 624, 12, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 11, 7892, 862, 1714, 315, 18368, 323, 4879, 43542, 382, 35, 58326, 510, 12, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 48284, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 374, 1865, 315, 81275, 624, 12, 47025, 304, 279, 22596, 1849, 13666, 4566, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 19853, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 5711, 43215, 320, 30956, 82, 8, 369, 8286, 18368, 624, 12, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 448, 82316, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 35753, 315, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 525, 43179, 323, 537, 21893, 8433, 624, 12, 576, 22596, 1849, 5711, 33213, 311, 29282, 17289, 11, 1393, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 33644, 389, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 369, 8286, 18368, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.129, -0.1603, -0.8718, -0.1295, -0.0002,