{"id": "647", "pred": "Cut", "raw_output": "To plant a sprouted potato, follow these steps:\n\n1. If the potato is large, cut it into chunks with two or three eyes each using a sharp knife, being careful not to break the long sprouts. Small potatoes can be planted whole.\n2. Place the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet and set them in a cool, dark location overnight so the cut ends can dry out.\n3. Prepare the planting area by turning the soil over to a depth of 12 inches and breaking it up finely. Remove any large rocks or debris.\n4. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep. If planting multiple rows, space them 24 to 36 inches apart.\n5. Place the potato chunks into the trench with the sprouted or eye side facing up, separating each cube by about 6 to 8 inches.\n6. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost, then replace the dirt on top.\n7. Water the potatoes thoroughly and continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch.\n8. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the vines to keep the soil cool and maintain consistent moisture.\n\nAnswer: Cut", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to plant a potato that has sprouted:\n\n1. Cut the sprouted potato into chunks with two or three eyes each, making sure to not break the long sprouts.\n2. Allow the cut ends to dry out overnight in a cool, dark location.\n3. Plant the potato chunks or whole potatoes in well-draining soil, spacing them 24 to 36 inches apart.\n4. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep, and place the potato pieces in the bottom of the trench with the sprouted side facing up.\n5. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings.\n\nNote that the passages do not provide specific information on how to care for the potatoes after planting, such as watering and fertilization.", "question": "how to plant a potato that has sprouted", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 83.17, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 6008, 264, 8151, 18533, 38734, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1416, 279, 38734, 374, 3460, 11, 3931, 432, 1119, 26757, 448, 1378, 476, 2326, 6414, 1817, 1667, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 1660, 16585, 537, 311, 1438, 279, 1293, 8151, 11672, 13, 14994, 34167, 646, 387, 38341, 4361, 624, 17, 13, 10771, 279, 38734, 26757, 389, 264, 34688, 476, 12544, 10834, 323, 738, 1105, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 6319, 3728, 24398, 773, 279, 3931, 10335, 646, 9058, 700, 624, 18, 13, 31166, 279, 47014, 3082, 553, 13054, 279, 17171, 916, 311, 264, 7990, 315, 220, 16, 17, 14924, 323, 14719, 432, 705, 60702, 13, 10783, 894, 3460, 23035, 476, 33998, 624, 19, 13, 37969, 264, 53252, 911, 220, 19, 14924, 6884, 323, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 5538, 13, 1416, 47014, 5248, 6978, 11, 3550, 1105, 220, 17, 19, 311, 220, 18, 21, 14924, 10747, 624, 20, 13, 10771, 279, 38734, 26757, 1119, 279, 53252, 448, 279, 8151, 18533, 476, 7912, 3108, 12880, 705, 11, 49445, 1817, 23739, 553, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 624, 21, 13, 17757, 279, 34167, 448, 264, 6193, 315, 56723, 11, 1221, 8290, 279, 25284, 389, 1909, 624, 22, 13, 9959, 279, 34167, 26364, 323, 3060, 72741, 15502, 979, 279, 17171, 374, 9058, 311, 279, 5796, 624, 23, 13, 2691, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 15602, 331, 2163, 279, 10779, 11, 22266, 432, 1182, 518, 3245, 220, 19, 14924, 504, 279, 85429, 311, 2506, 279, 17171, 7010, 323, 10306, 12966, 31157, 382, 16141, 25, 19649], "logp_list": [-0.1501, -0.0, -0.0019, -0.0233, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0143, -0.2814, -0.0005, -0.0015, -0.1673, -0.015, -0.0, -0.4204, -0.4182, -0.0574, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0028, -0.1003, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.6412, -0.0091, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0353, -0.3415, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0358, -0.2976, -0.0015, -0.0067, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0114, -0.0001, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0133, -0.0123, -0.001