{"id": "662", "pred": "- Final rinse for a shiny, healthy coat: Mix 1 cup of vinegar with 2–4 cups of water and use as a final rinse.\n- Normalize skin pH balance: Spray vinegar full-strength on the dog’s coat.\n- Improve skin and coat: Use apple cider vinegar (ACV) as a rinse.\n- Clean dog’s ears: Dilute apple cider vinegar with 50% water and apply with a cotton swab or gauze pad to soothe itchy ears.\n- Repel fleas: Spray ACV directly on the dog’s coat.\n- Bath in ACV-soap mixture to fight fleas.\n- Rinse the dog after treatment.", "raw_output": "- Final rinse for a shiny, healthy coat: Mix 1 cup of vinegar with 2–4 cups of water and use as a final rinse.\n- Normalize skin pH balance: Spray vinegar full-strength on the dog’s coat.\n- Improve skin and coat: Use apple cider vinegar (ACV) as a rinse.\n- Clean dog’s ears: Dilute apple cider vinegar with 50% water and apply with a cotton swab or gauze pad to soothe itchy ears.\n- Repel fleas: Spray ACV directly on the dog’s coat.\n- Bath in ACV-soap mixture to fight fleas.\n- Rinse the dog after treatment.", "gt": "Sure, I can answer your question based on the given passages. Here are some uses for vinegar for dogs:\n\n1. Coat and skin health: Mixing vinegar with water and using it as a final rinse can help to rejuvenate your dog's coat and balance their skin pH levels, according to Passage 1.\n2. Flea control: Vinegar can be used to repel fleas and remove them from your dog's coat, as mentioned in Passage 2.\n3. Itchy ears: Diluted vinegar can be used to soothe itchy ears, as stated in Passage 3.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions or if there's anything else I can assist you with.", "question": "vinegar uses for dogs", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 46.477, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [12, 13023, 73241, 369, 264, 41199, 11, 9314, 22875, 25, 