766, "input_len": 340, "output_tokens": 251, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 32.99, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "681", "pred": "By following these steps, you can obtain a free VoIP service and phone number.", "raw_output": "To get a free VoIP service and phone number, you can follow these steps based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Choose a VoIP service provider that offers free incoming numbers (DID or VoIP-In) from around the world. Some companies provide these for a flat yearly or monthly fee, but there are also free options available.\n\n2. Visit YouTube channels or online resources that guide you on obtaining free virtual phone numbers. For example, passage 2 mentions a YouTube channel (http://www.youtube.com/user/ricsil2037) that shows how to get a free Virtual Phone Number using VoIP.\n\n3. Get your free number from a respected company. Passage 2 specifically suggests Google as a company where you can get a free VoIP number.\n\n4. A VoIP number uses the internet to place and receive calls, so ensure you have a stable internet connection.\n\n5. Once you have the number, you can forward it to a mobile phone or use SIP devices to make outgoing calls, as mentioned in passage 3.\n\nBy following these steps, you can obtain a free VoIP service and phone number.", "gt": "To get a free VoIP service and phone number, you can visit YouTube channels which provide tutorials on how to access these services, such as the video available at http://www.youtube.com/user/ricsil2037. You could also use cloud VoIP services that require no equipment on your end. These services offer toll-free and US local numbers that can be forwarded to any US number or used with SIP devices for outgoing calls. Additionally, companies offer DID or incoming numbers from around the world either for a flat yearly rate or a monthly fee.", "question": "how to get free voip service and phone number", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 74.628, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_i