{"id": "683", "pred": "By following these steps, you can obtain a free VoIP service and phone number.", "raw_output": "To get a free VoIP service and phone number, you can follow these steps based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Choose a VoIP service provider that offers free incoming numbers (DID or VoIP-In) from around the world. Some companies provide these for a flat yearly or monthly fee, but there are also free options available.\n\n2. Visit YouTube channels or online resources that guide you on obtaining free virtual phone numbers. For example, passage 2 mentions a YouTube channel (http://www.youtube.com/user/ricsil2037) that shows how to get a free Virtual Phone Number using VoIP.\n\n3. Get your free number from a respected company. Passage 2 specifically suggests Google as a company where you can get a free VoIP number.\n\n4. A VoIP number uses the internet to place and receive calls, so ensure you have a stable internet connection.\n\n5. Once you have the number, you can forward it to a mobile phone or use SIP devices to make outgoing calls, as mentioned in passage 3.\n\nBy following these steps, you can obtain a free VoIP service and phone number.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to get free VoIP service and phone numbers:\n\n1. Free DID (incoming numbers) from around the world: There are several companies offering free or paid VoIP services that provide incoming numbers from around the world. These numbers can be obtained by signing up for a VoIP service provider and paying a flat yearly rate or monthly fee.\n2. Get a free Virtual Phone Number (VOIP) from Google: According to the passage, Google offers free virtual phone numbers that can be used to place and receive calls using the internet. To get a free number, visit the author's YouTube channel and follow the instructions provided.\n3. Cloud VoIP Service: The passage mentions a cloud VoIP service that provides toll-free numbers and US local numbers that can be forwarded to any US number (including cell phones) or used with a SIP device. While there is no direct mention of free service, the passage does indicate that the pricing has been lowered.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. None of the passages provide detailed information on how to get free VoIP service and phone numbers without any additional costs or requirements.", "question": "how to get free voip service and phone number", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 74.116, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 633, 264, 1910, 28079, 3298, 2473, 323, 4540, 1372, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 3118, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 22201, 264, 28079, 3298, 2473, 9109, 429, 6081, 1910, 19393, 5109, 320, 35, 915, 476, 28079, 3298, 31500, 8, 504, 2163, 279, 1879, 13, 4329, 5110, 3410, 1493, 369, 264, 10063, 44270, 476, 15088, 11060, 11, 714, 1052, 525, 1083, 1910, 2606, 2500, 382, 17, 13, 19008, 13370, 11744, 476, 2860, 4963, 429, 8474, 498, 389, 19009, 1910, 4108, 4540, 5109, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 21085, 220, 17, 33845, 264, 13370, 5496, 320, 1254, 1110, 2136, 20145, 905, 11739, 14, 6198, 321, 17, 15, 18, 22, 8, 429, 4933, 1246, 311, 633, 264, 1910, 20721, 14307, 5624, 1667, 28079, 3298, 382, 18, 13, 2126, 697, 1910, 1372, 504, 264, 30287, 2813, 13, 98475, 220, 17, 11689, 13230, 5085, 438, 264, 2813, 1380, 498, 646, 633, 264, 1910, 28079, 3298, 1372, 382, 19, 13, 362, 28079, 3298, 1372, 5711, 279, 7602, 311, 1992, 323, 5258, 6738, 11, 773, 5978, 498, 614, 264, 15175, 7602, 3633, 382, 20, 13, 9646, 498, 614, 279, 1372, 11, 498, 646, 4637, 432, 311, 264, 6371, 4540, 476, 990, 65441, 7611, 311, 1281, 36698, 6738, 11, 438, 9733, 304, 21085, 220, 18, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 6851, 264, 1910, 28079, 3298, 2473, 323, 4540, 1372, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2437, -0.0, -0.011, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0009, 0.0, -