{"id": "705", "pred": "Additionally, teachers can enhance learning by providing engaging materials and asking open-ended questions, modeling vocabulary, encouraging predictions, and observing children's activities.", "raw_output": "Children learn several things through water play:\n\n1. Gross motor skills: Running through sprinklers or filling and pouring water helps develop physical coordination and movement.\n2. Academic learning:\n   - Science: Children learn about floating and sinking and how different objects behave in water.\n   - Math: They learn about measuring, more and less by filling buckets with varying amounts of water.\n3. Creativity: Water play encourages imagination and pretend play.\n\nAdditionally, teachers can enhance learning by providing engaging materials and asking open-ended questions, modeling vocabulary, encouraging predictions, and observing children's activities.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, children learn the following through water play:\n\n1. Gross motor skills: Running, pouring, and manipulating water helps develop fine and gross motor skills. (Passage 1)\n2. Science concepts: Floating and sinking, measurement, and experimentation with different objects in water. (Passage 1)\n3. Creativity and imagination: Water play encourages children to use their imagination and engage in pretend play. (Passage 1)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not mention any other specific academic learning outcomes beyond gross motor skills, science concepts, and creativity.", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 39.181, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [11539, 3960, 3807, 2513, 1526, 3015, 1486, 1447, 16, 13, 42807, 8872, 7361, 25, 28025, 1526, 50698, 9254, 476, 21274, 323, 50413, 3015, 8609, 2225, 6961, 37693, 323, 7203, 624, 17, 13, 4