{"id": "709", "pred": "According to passage 1, the colors of the Tennessee flag have the following meanings:\n\n- White symbolizes purity.\n- Blue stands for the patriotism of the people of Tennessee.\n- Red stands for the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.\n\nThese colors—white, red, and blue—are noted as the national colors of the US.", "raw_output": "According to passage 1, the colors of the Tennessee flag have the following meanings:\n\n- White symbolizes purity.\n- Blue stands for the patriotism of the people of Tennessee.\n- Red stands for the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.\n\nThese colors—white, red, and blue—are noted as the national colors of the US.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nThe colors of the Tennessee flag have the following meanings:\n\n* White represents purity\n* Blue represents patriotism\n* Red represents the willingness to shed blood during warfare\n\nThe three white stars on the flag represent the three grand divisions of Tennessee: East, Middle, and West. The blue field with the white stars is meant to symbolize the three divisions bound together as one.", "question": "what do the colors of the tennessee flag mean", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 25.172, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [11190, 311, 21085, 220, 16, 11, 279, 7987, 315, 279, 23219, 5181, 614, 279, 2701, 49700, 1447, 12, 5807, 7735, 4756, 52400, 624, 12, 8697, 13352, 369, 279, 89342, 315, 279, 1251, 315, 23219, 624, 12, 3731, 13352, 369, 279, 61692, 315, 279, 1251, 311, 24354, 6543, 2337, 38207, 382, 9485, 7987, 2293, 5782, 11, 2518, 11, 323, 6303, 82772, 10342, 438, 279, 5313, 7987, 315, 279, 2274, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1887, -0.0, -0.2032, -0.0, -0.0, -0.003, -0.0305, -0.0027, -0.0233, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0067, -0.0234, -0.5653, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0