{"id": "719", "pred": "The PoachPod® can also be placed in the dishwasher for easy cleanup.", "raw_output": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, follow these steps:\n\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Lightly oil the silicone PoachPod® (as mentioned in passage 3).\n3. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone pod, being careful not to break the yolk.\n4. Carefully float the PoachPod® in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod.\n5. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for six minutes (as per passage 2) or about 4–6 minutes (as per passage 3).\n6. After cooking, remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod® out of the hot water.\n7. Flip the PoachPod® upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed poached egg onto the plate.\n\nThe PoachPod® can also be placed in the dishwasher for easy cleanup.", "gt": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n\n1. Begin by bringing a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Gently slide an egg into your silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the egg's yolk.\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring that the pod stays upright and no water gets inside.\n4. Cover the pot with a tight-fitting lid and allow the egg to cook for 6 minutes.\n5. After 6 minutes, remove the lid from the pot and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to carefully lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 69.346, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 3193, 610, 458, 18636, 1667, 264, 13808, 610, 23527, 66357, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 39124, 264, 34