{"id": "720", "pred": "The PoachPod® can also be placed in the dishwasher for easy cleanup.", "raw_output": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, follow these steps:\n\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Lightly oil the silicone PoachPod® (as mentioned in passage 3).\n3. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone pod, being careful not to break the yolk.\n4. Carefully float the PoachPod® in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod.\n5. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for six minutes (as per passage 2) or about 4–6 minutes (as per passage 3).\n6. After cooking, remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod® out of the hot water.\n7. Flip the PoachPod® upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed poached egg onto the plate.\n\nThe PoachPod® can also be placed in the dishwasher for easy cleanup.", "gt": "Sure! Here's how to poach an egg using a PoachPod® based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil. (Passage 1)\n2. Carefully crack an egg into the PoachPod®, being careful not to break the yolk. (Passage 2)\n3. Gently slide the PoachPod® into the boiling water, making sure it floats upright and no water enters the pod. (Passage 2)\n4. Cover the pot with a lid and cook for 6 minutes. (Passage 2)\n5. Use a large slotted spoon or tongs to carefully remove the PoachPod® from the water and flip it upside down over a plate. (Passage 2)\n6. Press gently on the bottom of the PoachPod® to release the poached egg onto the plate. (Passage 2)\n\nThat's it! According to the passages, the PoachPod® makes it easy to poach eggs by allowing you to float them in boiling water without breaking the yolk. Just make sure to lightly oil the pod before adding the egg to prevent sticking.", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "h