{"id": "722", "pred": "The PoachPod® can also be placed in the dishwasher for easy cleanup.", "raw_output": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, follow these steps:\n\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Lightly oil the silicone PoachPod® (as mentioned in passage 3).\n3. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone pod, being careful not to break the yolk.\n4. Carefully float the PoachPod® in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod.\n5. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for six minutes (as per passage 2) or about 4–6 minutes (as per passage 3).\n6. After cooking, remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod® out of the hot water.\n7. Flip the PoachPod® upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed poached egg onto the plate.\n\nThe PoachPod® can also be placed in the dishwasher for easy cleanup.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to poach an egg using a PoachPod®:\n\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Crack an egg into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the yolk.\n3. Gently slide the pod into the boiling water, making sure it stays upright and no water gets in.\n4. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for 6 minutes.\n5. Use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and press the bottom to release the poached egg.\n\nSo, to summarize, the steps to poach an egg using a PoachPod® are:\n\n1. Bring water to a boil.\n2. Crack egg into pod.\n3. Float pod in boiling water.\n4. Cook for 6 minutes.\n5. Remove pod from water.\n6. Release egg onto plate.", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 68.959, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 3193, 6