{"id": "735", "pred": "The difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS (Short Message Service) only allows you to send text messages with a maximum of 160 characters per message, and longer messages are split into parts. In contrast, MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that allows you to send multimedia content such as pictures, videos, audio, and text, either individually or in combination. MMS messages can carry larger content sizes, up to 300KB, and support formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF.", "raw_output": "The difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS (Short Message Service) only allows you to send text messages with a maximum of 160 characters per message, and longer messages are split into parts. In contrast, MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that allows you to send multimedia content such as pictures, videos, audio, and text, either individually or in combination. MMS messages can carry larger content sizes, up to 300KB, and support formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF.", "gt": "SMS stands for Short Message Service, commonly referred to as a text message, and allows you to send a text message of up to 160 characters to another device. MMS, which stands for Multimedia Messaging Service, is an evolution of SMS. It allows you to send messages that include pictures, video, or audio content to another device. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB. SMS is restricted to sending text-only messages, whereas MMS allows a combination of text, pictures, sounds, and videos.", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 37.753, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 374, 429, 29909, 320, 12472, 4856, 5362, 8, 1172, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 1467, 6605, 448, 264, 7192, 315, 220, 16, 21, 15, 5766, 81