{"id": "737", "pred": "The difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS (Short Message Service) only allows you to send text messages with a maximum of 160 characters per message, and longer messages are split into parts. In contrast, MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that allows you to send multimedia content such as pictures, videos, audio, and text, either individually or in combination. MMS messages can carry larger content sizes, up to 300KB, and support formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF.", "raw_output": "The difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS (Short Message Service) only allows you to send text messages with a maximum of 160 characters per message, and longer messages are split into parts. In contrast, MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that allows you to send multimedia content such as pictures, videos, audio, and text, either individually or in combination. MMS messages can carry larger content sizes, up to 300KB, and support formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, SMS stands for Short Message Service and allows you to send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. In contrast, MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows you to send a message including pictures, videos, sounds, text, or any combination of the four. The content of an MMS message has a maximum size of 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, GIF, etc.", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "cad", "has_cad": true, "cad_context": "passage", "time_sec": 37.783, "status": "success", "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 374, 429, 29909, 320, 12472, 4856, 5362, 8, 1172, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 1467, 6605, 448, 264, 7192, 315, 220, 16, 21, 15, 5766, 817, 1943, 11, 323, 5021, 6605, 525, 6718, 1119, 5479, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 386, 4826, 320, 40404, 26936, 73170, 5362, 8, 374, 4